":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/6a70b22f39115ad35768fc227df722946bc1a4f2","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDZhNzBiMjJmMzkxMTVhZDM1NzY4ZmMyMjdkZjcyMjk0NmJjMWE0ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/310bb7bb0c86f3ba9ea327eff0c2a9e71801241f","sha":"310bb7bb0c86f3ba9ea327eff0c2a9e71801241f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/310bb7bb0c86f3ba9ea327eff0c2a9e71801241f"}],"sha":"6a70b22f39115ad35768fc227df722946bc1a4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/6a70b22f39115ad35768fc227df722946bc1a4f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/310bb7bb0c86f3ba9ea327eff0c2a9e71801241f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:43:41Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:43:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): resolve open Dependabot alerts (#1571)\n\n* fix(shared): bump vulnerable dependencies\n\nnodemailer 10.0.15, undici 7.29.1, axios 1.20.0, multer 2.4.0,\nip-address 10.7.1, js-yaml 5.4.1, brace-expansion 5.0.12,\nfast-uri 4.2.1, moment 2.31.0.\n\nnodemailer 10 ships its own types, where SentMessageInfo is no longer\nany, so sendMail now declares the ResultWrapper it already returned.\n\n* fix(regulations): upgrade file-type to 21\n\nfile-type 16 hangs on a malformed ASF upload (GHSA-5v7r-6r5c-r473).\n21 is ESM-only: the built service loads it through Node 24''s\nrequire(esm), and jest now transforms it with the rest of the\nESM-only deps in jest.preset.js.\n\n* fix(ojoi): move pdfjs-dist off the vulnerable 3.x line\n\npdfjs-dist 3.11 runs attacker JS from a crafted font\n(GHSA-wgrm-67xf-hhpq). It came in through react-pdf 7, declared by\nojoi-modules for two different consumers:\n\n- PdfService only used react-pdf to find pdfjs. It now depends on\n  pdfjs-dist ^4.10.38 directly, loads the ESM legacy build, and sets\n  isEvalSupported: false, the upstream mitigation. disableWorker was\n  ignored since pdfjs 3.\n- island-ui core''s PdfViewer imports react-pdf, which the web apps only\n  had because of that hoisted declaration. @dmr.is/ui now declares\n  react-pdf 9.1.0, the version island.is pins (pdfjs-dist 4.4.168).\n\n* fix(shared): carry resolutions into images and tidy sendMail callers\n\nReview of #1571:\n- Should fix 1: the images install with npm and no lockfile, which ignores\n  Yarn''s resolutions. scripts/docker/prepare-package-json.js now writes them\n  into dist/package.json as npm overrides in all 13 Dockerfiles, and is a\n  shared global so editing it rebuilds every container.\n- Should fix 2: doe-mail''s sendMailResult returns the declared\n  ResultWrapper instead of narrowing an `any`; stale comments and the\n  bare-value specs go with it.\n- Should fix 3: a spec loads pdfjs''s ESM legacy build in a real Node child\n  process and extracts text, as PdfService does.\n- Optional 1: axios pinned as nx/axios.\n- Optional 2: ojoi-modules pins pdfjs-dist 4.4.168, react-pdf''s version, so\n  only one copy is installed.\n- Optional 3: dmr-ui README says why it declares react-pdf.\n- Optional 4: the LG listener spec mocks real ResultWrappers.\n- Optional 5: OJ case/comment and LG listener read sendMail''s err result\n  instead of a catch that could never run.\n\n* fix(shared): keep resolution floors in images and test the mail branches\n\nSecond review of #1571:\n- Should fix 1: a top-level resolution that names a direct dependency now\n  also raises that dependency to the pin before `$name` refers to it, as\n  Yarn applies it, so an image can never install below the floor.\n- Optional 1: only the pkg.pr.new builds are skipped; `npm:<range>` is\n  unwrapped, and any other protocol spec throws instead of vanishing.\n- Optional 2: the script reads the resolutions Nx already copies into\n  dist/package.json, so the Dockerfiles no longer copy the root one, and\n  it is a container-target input rather than a shared global. Covered by\n  node:test specs in the deploy-scripts job.\n- Optional 3: aws.service.spec pins that a failed SES send resolves an\n  err result, and comment.service.spec covers both email branches.\n- Optional 4: the pdfjs spec has a timeout, reads the specifier from\n  pdf.service.ts and the options from PDFJS_DOCUMENT_OPTIONS.\n\n* fix(shared): keep exact direct versions and refuse npm-less selectors\n\nThird review of #1571:\n- Optional 1: the pkg.pr.new comment says what is true: web images take\n  the registry vanilla-extract, as they always have.\n- Optional 2: a direct spec that already sits inside a range pin is kept,\n  so exact versions stay exact; an exact pin, or a spec outside the\n  range, still raises the dependency to the pin.\n- Optional 3: `**` and `pkg@range` selectors throw, since npm overrides\n  cannot express them.\n- Optional 4: the err sendMail spec asserts SES was reached.\n\n* docs(shared): say a resolution can replace a direct spec, not only raise it","tree":{"sha":"0fb47d001873aaab55290d3031414d02724ebb88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/0fb47d001873aaab55290d3031414d02724ebb88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/310bb7bb0c86f3ba9ea327eff0c2a9e71801241f","verification":{"payload":"tree 0fb47d001873aaab55290d3031414d02724ebb88\nparent ad0544cc32022a7a40584e3ef5da315ec1c69fbd\nauthor Jón Bjarni Ólafsson <dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com> 1791449021 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791449021 +0000\n\nfix(shared): resolve open Dependabot alerts (#1571)\n\n* fix(shared): bump vulnerable dependencies\n\nnodemailer 10.0.15, undici 7.29.1, axios 1.20.0, multer 2.4.0,\nip-address 10.7.1, js-yaml 5.4.1, brace-expansion 5.0.12,\nfast-uri 4.2.1, moment 2.31.0.\n\nnodemailer 10 ships its own types, where SentMessageInfo is no longer\nany, so sendMail now declares the ResultWrapper it already returned.\n\n* fix(regulations): upgrade file-type to 21\n\nfile-type 16 hangs on a malformed ASF upload (GHSA-5v7r-6r5c-r473).\n21 is ESM-only: the built service loads it through Node 24''s\nrequire(esm), and jest now transforms it with the rest of the\nESM-only deps in jest.preset.js.\n\n* fix(ojoi): move pdfjs-dist off the vulnerable 3.x line\n\npdfjs-dist 3.11 runs attacker JS from a crafted font\n(GHSA-wgrm-67xf-hhpq). It came in through react-pdf 7, declared by\nojoi-modules for two different consumers:\n\n- PdfService only used react-pdf to find pdfjs. It now depends on\n  pdfjs-dist ^4.10.38 directly, loads the ESM legacy build, and sets\n  isEvalSupported: false, the upstream mitigation. disableWorker was\n  ignored since pdfjs 3.\n- island-ui core''s PdfViewer imports react-pdf, which the web apps only\n  had because of that hoisted declaration. @dmr.is/ui now declares\n  react-pdf 9.1.0, the version island.is pins (pdfjs-dist 4.4.168).\n\n* fix(shared): carry resolutions into images and tidy sendMail callers\n\nReview of #1571:\n- Should fix 1: the images install with npm and no lockfile, which ignores\n  Yarn''s resolutions. scripts/docker/prepare-package-json.js now writes them\n  into dist/package.json as npm overrides in all 13 Dockerfiles, and is a\n  shared global so editing it rebuilds every container.\n- Should fix 2: doe-mail''s sendMailResult returns the declared\n  ResultWrapper instead of narrowing an `any`; stale comments and the\n  bare-value specs go with it.\n- Should fix 3: a spec loads pdfjs''s ESM legacy build in a real Node child\n  process and extracts text, as PdfService does.\n- Optional 1: axios pinned as nx/axios.\n- Optional 2: ojoi-modules pins pdfjs-dist 4.4.168, react-pdf''s version, so\n  only one copy is installed.\n- Optional 3: dmr-ui README says why it declares react-pdf.\n- Optional 4: the LG listener spec mocks real ResultWrappers.\n- Optional 5: OJ case/comment and LG listener read sendMail''s err result\n  instead of a catch that could never run.\n\n* fix(shared): keep resolution floors in images and test the mail branches\n\nSecond review of #1571:\n- Should fix 1: a top-level resolution that names a direct dependency now\n  also raises that dependency to the pin before `$name` refers to it, as\n  Yarn applies it, so an image can never install below the floor.\n- Optional 1: only the pkg.pr.new builds are skipped; `npm:<range>` is\n  unwrapped, and any other protocol spec throws instead of vanishing.\n- Optional 2: the script reads the resolutions Nx already copies into\n  dist/package.json, so the Dockerfiles no longer copy the root one, and\n  it is a container-target input rather than a shared global. Covered by\n  node:test specs in the deploy-scripts job.\n- Optional 3: aws.service.spec pins that a failed SES send resolves an\n  err result, and comment.service.spec covers both email branches.\n- Optional 4: the pdfjs spec has a timeout, reads the specifier from\n  pdf.service.ts and the options from PDFJS_DOCUMENT_OPTIONS.\n\n* fix(shared): keep exact direct versions and refuse npm-less selectors\n\nThird review of #1571:\n- Optional 1: the pkg.pr.new comment says what is true: web images take\n  the registry vanilla-extract, as they always have.\n- Optional 2: a direct spec that already sits inside a range pin is kept,\n  so exact versions stay exact; an exact pin, or a spec outside the\n  range, still raises the dependency to the pin.\n- Optional 3: `**` and `pkg@range` selectors throw, since npm overrides\n  cannot express them.\n- Optional 4: the err sendMail spec asserts SES was reached.\n\n* docs(shared): say a resolution can replace a direct spec, not only raise it","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1e9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPaQQACt/S/Clce9SaO/3cFXsNhAB\nK2FtE7Bpjnhn9UvZl+efik2vXQg455iI0VALPOw/Qkbm0PBTh4V4YrvohJKxpDKa\nJSDaQcOo5O6CnnN6Tz6JPvcAH5C8/hYfoVNNO6IgbfuQNNEToe/teWmYIRVtET0p\nAqEly4skN5n9/57d+2sTEwtw6oRkLFrWEOQoGSZ3D87/EddxSM/Ip65KYc+oqqxB\nwQRsX1JijX7zgyuWJu2XztwhXITCm7iVMVFWCx+mNX6J4L29t8IgYttLj64SR1TK\niyx1BXU1qhCeDH/EfPv2gLt3w13gSFarSRrD0AUp9U/MzDXoPGJjrRzjzOA99f+5\nE16Y2TBh8iRW3owODWghI1tSkiLfx21TizB7utIrW0Bt0OD2pmPfE0FNZiLyrmr3\nexrM5N9D4EI2oYIwFhkSoIa7xTQBxRHBK1j4WoqQrGvtZQ2SEwfxoIAAl83zxsAZ\nIC6kB09oQpQiDRZ5nXiZIgeOXjQAueeVteJOCfyOAMbyoxcbSOm8Wq5LVR9VP2KY\nqdJUhZWEMemYgv3Z+WJtTJqXTwfoudLGReSO3WVeCuKiSCuJbsiW3z9zznEnkoII\nJYOxjRDpiyKZ9OXJu4BJ30BxosCJeW4BOqMeWIPYT2t8Yk7tn7Y31i5YkEMb