ps://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/aebb5600fcd941528b07148b80e63e660440229a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:06:40Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:06:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ojoi): sync published advert title when publishing a correction (#1570)\n\n* fix(ojoi): sync published advert title when publishing a correction\n\nEditing \"Heiti auglýsingar\" on a published case only updated the case,\nso the regenerated PDF showed the new title while the published advert\nkept the old subject. Publishing a correction now writes the case''s\nadvertTitle to the advert''s subject.\n\nThe correction''s own title was previously forwarded as `title`, which\nthe advert update mapper ignores; it stays on the correction record only.\n\n* fix(ojoi): reindex the advert after publishing a correction\n\nA correction rewrites the published advert''s HTML, title and possibly\npublication date, but only publishing triggered a search reindex, so\nsearch kept serving the pre-correction document. Reindex after the\ncorrection commits, the same way publishing does. A reindex failure is\nlogged and never fails the correction.\n\n* test(ojoi): restore correction spec stubs after each test\n\nThe overrides used Object.assign on module instances shared across the\nfile, which jest.restoreAllMocks() does not undo. Use jest.spyOn on\ndefault jest.fn() methods so the existing afterEach restores them.","tree":{"sha":"f04450a21adb9001ed4e7a66247b74a25ea428a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/f04450a21adb9001ed4e7a66247b74a25ea428a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/aebb5600fcd941528b07148b80e63e660440229a","verification":{"payload":"tree f04450a21adb9001ed4e7a66247b74a25ea428a0\nparent a57052ccc6bcd2a2b2992a522a4c8893117d7eff\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1791382000 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791382000 +0000\n\nfix(ojoi): sync published advert title when publishing a correction (#1570)\n\n* fix(ojoi): sync published advert title when publishing a correction\n\nEditing \"Heiti auglýsingar\" on a published case only updated the case,\nso the regenerated PDF showed the new title while the published advert\nkept the old subject. Publishing a correction now writes the case''s\nadvertTitle to the advert''s subject.\n\nThe correction''s own title was previously forwarded as `title`, which\nthe advert update mapper ignores; it stays on the correction record only.\n\n* fix(ojoi): reindex the advert after publishing a correction\n\nA correction rewrites the published advert''s HTML, title and possibly\npublication date, but only publishing triggered a search reindex, so\nsearch kept serving the pre-correction document. Reindex after the\ncorrection commits, the same way publishing does. A reindex failure is\nlogged and never fails the correction.\n\n* test(ojoi): restore correction spec stubs after each test\n\nThe overrides used Object.assign on module instances shared across the\nfile, which jest.restoreAllMocks() does not undo. Use jest.spyOn on\ndefault jest.fn() methods so the existing afterEach restores them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxlHwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzOEQAAkhXzEoToiqUTKrs2EmaM1O\ne5NBgj9j5X0gdkkbmJweqRi5nQ5fpvpJjhO053azoBmYdnwWEtObaKfIKjj2dip/\n4JrlqWyKKwS/rppVWhSOtgk6muDnfu3vWQhGrXMxO/r/dcmzCRuKEtZUPPUR0wSk\nUrJom9pBkApOloBN57URQKyJVzEu73fr7OApUVZHq3c34jmu8fk4fa9AOEIVHzs1\nsUNzUFkuCBLuGp45MSvAgYV+rhGNMnzqjLjuhzlSRG2F/juDbOrIzxNCNLKIAekn\nM/k92pUJ0Y8X5yQ0SXQ/jI+4705VMBuzRk7p1dn/S8fgAKq1tjlDXve94E7/OKE4\nwQjJy7KWVGSdFa66Vk7OXaLX85prWAB5PtsF880i8XqsZKiqkOeS9Rr2jMmdCEm4\n9rXS6SeAZVjQfwlqo8qIpS3UuCLX1GLDdsBheR8ZhwWCKU12gs1DBCpuNzrdfpO/\n1/tD+qPc3XySk/RN1PXCBNydE1i961ALz99YhqREQfqRFkSJ31bUi0pDGS3vbTmz\nXCiHj3TrxyV7SD9d0Ryaxoe2FtU1mFn4sWRrZe9n+5WyRpp0OyT81EmzSgt6yyVR\nhbws+Q7jJrcEZ8uX4ONS84eKYpbMrlnUO2O2uHKjrjzGn4FcVC9jWKrAb0BRpqfu\nBZ3jXkQsKOepRNKhVrjW\n=v/KC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:06:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/aebb5600fcd941528b07148b80e63e660440229a","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGFlYmI1NjAwZmNkOTQxNTI4YjA3MTQ4YjgwZTYzZTY2MDQ0MDIyOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/a57052ccc6bcd2a2b2992a522a4c8893117d7eff","sha":"a57052ccc6bcd2a2b2992a522a4c8893117d7eff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/a57052ccc6bcd2a2b2992a522a4c8893117d7eff"}],"sha":"aebb5600fcd941528b07148b80e63e660440229a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/aebb5600fcd941528b07148b80e63e660440229a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/a57052ccc6bcd2a2b2992a522a4c8893117d7eff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:49:59Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:49:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(doe): partner API manual test findings (#1559)\n\n* chore(doe): open partner API manual test findings\n\n* fix(shared): name 409, 413 and 429 errors and keep body-parser 4xx out of 500\n\nHttpExceptionFilter gave ConflictException, PayloadTooLargeException and\nThrottlerException the generic ''An unexpected error occurred.'' body with no\nname. Match them by status and name them.\n\nA body-parser refusal (too large, malformed JSON) is an http-errors instance,\nnot an HttpException, so GlobalExceptionFilter answered it with 500. Keep an\nexposed 4xx status and say what was refused.\n\n* fix(doe): read the equality payload part past the global pipe\n\nThe global ValidationPipe runs before param pipes and takes its metatype from\nthe parameter''s DTO annotation, so it validated the raw multipart string\nagainst SubmitPartnerEqualityReportDto and refused every equality submission.\nRead the part with a custom param decorator, which global pipes skip, and let\nJsonPartPipe do the whole job.\n\nSplit main.ts''s app setup into configureApp and add an HTTP-level spec that\nruns requests through it, since the controller spec calls handlers directly\nand never met the global pipe.\n\n* fix(doe): refuse an unknown subsidiary kennitala with 400, not 502\n\ngetOrCreateSubsidiaryReportSnapshotSource used getEntityByNationalId, which\nturns the registry''s 404 for a kennitala it does not hold into a 502, so its\nown not-found branch was unreachable and a filer''s bad subsidiary read as our\nfailure. Use findEntityByNationalId and answer with a 400 naming the\nsubsidiary.\n\nValidate the subsidiary kennitala''s shape and checksum at the DTO, accepting\nand stripping the dash, so a malformed one never reaches the registry.\n\n* fix(doe): return the employee score on filed outlier rows\n\nApplicationService.getReportOutliers loaded reportEmployee without score, so\nevery outlier row on the island.is and partner channels read score: null\nalthough the column is populated at submit. Load it, as the admin\nReportService already does.\n\n* fix(doe): refuse a whitespace-only outlier explanation\n\nminLength: 1 let ''   '' stand as a group''s reason, action or signature, so a\nreport moved to SUBMITTED with a blank explanation. Trim the four text fields\nof the filing and edit DTOs before validating, as the draft flow already\ndoes.\n\n* fix(doe): refuse page and pageSize below 1, cap partner pages at 100\n\nPagingQuery accepted pageSize=0, which answered an empty page with\ntotalPages null and a nextPage that led nowhere, and page=0, an offset below\nzero. Refuse both with @Min(1) on the shared DTO. No upper bound there, since\nadmin screens read whole registers through it.\n\nThe partner outliers route takes PartnerPagingQuery, which also caps pageSize\nat PAGING_MAXIMUM_PAGE_SIZE.\n\n* fix(doe): take last month at the latest as the salary data period\n\nThe current month counted as soon as it had started, though its payroll is\nnot all paid until it is over. Move the window''s latest month back by one on\nevery write path, keep its earliest bound, and start the admin month picker\nat last month to match.\n\n* test(doe): build kennitala fixtures deterministically\n\ngenerateCompany and generatePerson pick a random serial, which made the\nvalidator spec fail intermittently in a full run.\n\n* fix(doe): refuse kennitala identifiers, negative pay and bad employee fields\n\nEvery channel accepted a checksum-valid kennitala as an employee''s\nidentifier, which reviewers see beside every flagged row, and also negative\nor fractional ordinals, negative pay components and a start date in the\nfuture or off the calendar.\n\nCheck them in the payload integrity pass, where the island.is, partner and\nworkbook paths converge, and restate the start-date and pay rules on the\ndraft employee DTOs, which never pass through it.\n\n* fix(doe): refuse bad contact addresses, a blank phone and negative averages\n\nEvery report write DTO took companyAdminEmail and contactEmail as any\nstring, contactPhone as \"\", and the three average employee counts as any\nnumber, so ''notanemail'' and -5 filed with 201. Require an address, a phone\nwith text once trimmed, and averages of at least zero on the island.is,\npartner, admin and direct-create DTOs. Fractions stay: a twelve-month\naverage is fractional.\n\nThe draft header restates the rules but lets an address stay blank while\nthe draft is being filled in.\n\n* fix(doe): refuse an unknown ÍSAT code or postcode on partner filings\n\nThe company snapshot''s isatCategory and postcode are free text, so 99.99 and\n99999 filed with 201. On the partner channel, require each to lead with a\ncode in our reference tables. The ÍSAT code may be dotted, undotted, a class\nrather than a subclass, or followed by its description, so real filings are\nnot refused for how they write it.\n\nisland.is keeps the free text: it sends formats we have not catalogued, and\nrefusing them there would refuse filings that never failed before.\n\n* fix(doe): stop naming the stored providerId in 409s\n\nA taken providerId answered \"Provider tuple (OTHER, \"5005101370:mt-eq-empty\")\nis already registered for a EQUALITY report\", which showed a partner the\nkennitala-namespaced form the guide says it never sees, and named the type\nby its enum. Say the providerId is already used by a different company or\nfor an equality or salary report, and log the stored tuple instead.\n\n* fix(doe): answer a partner replay before reading its body\n\nThe guide says a replay''s body is not read, but a used equality providerId\nsent with a PDF got 400: the document was converted before the shared path\nreached its replay check. A salary replay likewise ran the scoring-model\nexpansion and the snapshot checks first, so a deleted model 404''d it.\n\nLook the tuple up first on both partner submissions and return the replay,\nor its 409, before anything else runs.\n\n* fix(doe): say whose approval a vendor''s missing scope needs\n\nA vendor refused because its firm is not approved for a scope, or because\nthe company did not grant it, was told \"API key is missing the … scope\",\nwhich sends it to reissue a key that is fine. Keep the firm''s own scopes\nbeside the narrowed ones and name the firm''s approval or the company''s\ngrant, whichever lacks it. A company key''s refusal is unchanged.\n\n* fix(doe): name sub-criteria by title in job assignment refusals\n\nSetting a job''s step assignments refused with messages quoting the sub-criterion\nand step UUIDs („80e8107e-…“ er einstaklingsbundið), which tell an employer\nnothing about their own model. Name the sub-criterion as \"criterion / sub\",\nthe form the submission validator uses, and an id that is not in the model by\nits place in the array, since it has no title.\n\n* fix(doe): count a duplicate-titled sub-criterion in both weight totals\n\nThe model validator dropped a sub-criterion whose title repeated another''s\nbefore running the submission gate, but kept its criterion''s derived weight.\nCRITERIA then summed a weight SUB_CRITERIA did not, so one model reported\n102.2345% and 101.2345%, and jobs assigned on the duplicate were told their\nassignment no longer existed. Report the duplicate, then keep it under a\ngate-only title so both totals and its assignments see it.\n\n* fix(doe): answer a scoring model delete with 204\n\nDELETE /partner/scoring-models/{modelId} answered 200 with an empty body.\nNothing is left to return, so say so with 204, in the route, its OpenAPI\nresponse and the guide. The part DELETEs keep 200 with the remaining model.\n\n* docs(doe): bring the partner guide up to date with the shipped self-service web\n\nThe guide still said the self-service web was being built, that no customer\ncould connect yet and that Jafnréttisstofa issued vendor keys meanwhile; it\nshipped in #1552. A customer connecting \"chooses what to allow\", though\naccess has been all or nothing since #1554. And \"covers enough employees\"\npromised a check that is only at least one employee.\n\n* fix(doe): rename a duplicate sub-criterion for the gate with a suffix no title has\n\nThe gate renamed a duplicate \"A\" to \"A (2)\", which collides with a real\n\"A (2)\" in the same criterion, reported that one as a duplicate the employer\nnever made, and put a title they never wrote into gate messages. Suffix NUL\nand a number instead, which a Postgres text column cannot hold, and strip it\nfrom every gate message.\n\n* refactor(doe): drop the unused IsNotKennitala decorator\n\nThe identifier rule runs in the payload integrity pass through\nisKennitalaLike, and the draft employee DTOs carry no identifier, so the\ndecorator had no field to guard. Test isKennitalaLike directly instead.\n\n* fix(doe): keep the salary data window at 36 finished months\n\nTaking last month as the latest moved the window''s newest month back by one\nbut left its oldest, so it held 35 months while the 400, the DTO\ndescriptions and the guide still said 36, and a filer who chose the month\nexactly 36 back was refused by a message saying it fit. Move the oldest\nmonth back too, and have the admin picker offer all 36.\n\n* fix(doe): strip the gate title suffix without a control-character regex\n\n/\\u0000\\d+/ tripped no-control-regex and failed linting. Split the message\non the NUL mark and drop the number that follows it instead.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kristinn Þorri Þrastarson <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"472a20fbda87af4d231b1083b3f95096efad139f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/472a20fbda87af4d231b1083b3f95096efad139f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/a57052ccc6bcd2a2b2992a522a4c8893117d7eff","verification":{"payload":"tree 472a20fbda87af4d231b1083b3f95096efad139f\nparent 1b46666d7a98cb03130906b187fbc1f28a35396d\nauthor Jón Bjarni Ólafsson <dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com> 1791380999 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791380999 +0000\n\nfix(doe): partner API manual test findings (#1559)\n\n* chore(doe): open partner API manual test findings\n\n* fix(shared): name 409, 413 and 429 errors and keep body-parser 4xx out of 500\n\nH