"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/18ad1643743f39530845923cb0314d039964c4da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:05:06Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"fix: sticky bar and cleanup","tree":{"sha":"ad16d7aa238898c69bd05238cccf14a9d02c9ed9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/ad16d7aa238898c69bd05238cccf14a9d02c9ed9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/18ad1643743f39530845923cb0314d039964c4da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/18ad1643743f39530845923cb0314d039964c4da","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDE4YWQxNjQzNzQzZjM5NTMwODQ1OTIzY2IwMzE0ZDAzOTk2NGM0ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d","sha":"15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d"}],"sha":"18ad1643743f39530845923cb0314d039964c4da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/18ad1643743f39530845923cb0314d039964c4da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:57:14Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"refactor(doe): collapse the export tabs into one company list\n\nThe screen had two datasets and the admins only act on one of them. A list of\nfilings was a second thing to reconcile against the register rather than an\nanswer in its own right, and it forced two row units, two tables and two\nexport files through one screen.\n\nNow there is one dataset — companies — and the report filters NARROW it. A\ncompany comes back when at least one of its filings satisfies every report\ncriterion given, and it appears once however many of its reports match. Every\nrow is still a company, and the file keeps its company columns.\n\nTwo decisions this rests on:\n\nAPPROVED filings only. A draft was never sent, a denied one was rejected and\na withdrawn one was taken back — none is something the Directorate accepted,\nand counting them would let a company answer \"has filed a skýrslugjöf with a\ngap under 4%\" on the strength of a submission that was turned down. That also\nremoves report status as a criterion: there is one status these can have, so\na control offering it would be inert. Communication status goes with it — it\ndescribes a filing still in flight.\n\nEvery criterion applies to the SAME filing. Asking for a skýrslugjöf approved\nin 2026 with a 10–15% gap finds companies with one filing that is all three,\nnot companies with three filings that are each one of them. Hence a single\ncorrelated EXISTS rather than one per criterion.\n\n`CompanyFilter` gains a children slot so the report cards render inside its\nown Filter shell rather than beside a second one. A slot and not more props:\nthreading each report criterion through would make that component''s signature\nthe union of every screen that uses it, and the register wants none of them.\n\nCaught while testing: a NaN bound made the whole clause degrade to \"has any\napproved filing\" instead of being refused, because `hasReportCriteria` and the\npredicate disagreed about what counted as set. Both now go through one\n`finiteBound`. Silently widening a result is the worst of the three available\nbehaviours — it looks like data.\n\n`/api/v1/export/reports` stays. Nothing in the UI calls it now, but it is a\nworking, tested, documented surface and the reports data is still real.","tree":{"sha":"81e23e50ce89183ea2f734545fbe6e987438c0ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/81e23e50ce89183ea2f734545fbe6e987438c0ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDE1ZDg3NjM3ZmQ2YzY3MjRiZjhmNzYxNWJmYTk3ZWVhNDMzNzk1OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2","sha":"b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2"}],"sha":"15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/15d87637fd6c6724bf8f7615bfa97eea4337958d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:25:25Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"feat(doe): add admin gender, pay-gap ranges and \"Aldrei innsent\" filters\n\nThree filters, plus the schema refresh that was outstanding.\n\n**Kyn æðsta stjórnanda** on Skýrslur. Reads `report.company_admin_gender`,\nwhich is frozen at submission like the rest of the filing — it says who\nsigned off on THAT report, not who holds the post today.\n\n**Launamunur** on Skýrslur, as TWO ranges rather than one. Óleiðréttur and\nóskýrður differ by roughly a factor of three on the same company, and only\nthe second is tested against the benchmark, so a single control labelled\n\"Launamunur\" would let an admin ask one question and read the other''s answer.\nBoth are named in full on the control and in the exported file''s filter\nsheet. Bounds step by 0,5 from \"Enginn launamunur\" to 15, offered as frá/til\nselects rather than 31 buckets — \"5% and up\" and \"between 2 and 4\" are the\nquestions people actually ask, and a bucket list makes those the awkward\nones.\n\nThe figures live in a JSONB column, so the filter is a correlated EXISTS with\nthe value extracted and cast. `IS NOT NULL` there is load-bearing rather than\ndefensive: an equality plan has no gap and a single-gender workforce has no\nmeasurable one, and neither may answer \"show me 0–0,5%\" — a gap that cannot\nbe computed is not a gap of zero.\n\n**Aldrei innsent** on Fyrirtæki, not Skýrslur. A company with no filing has\nno report row, so it can never appear in a list whose unit is the filing; on\nthe register it is a flag alongside Dagsektir and Skiladagur liðinn. It also\nexcludes companies carried over from the retired register — a SharePoint-era\ncertification IS a submission, and without that half the filter would caption\n~600 certified companies \"never submitted\", which is false and the opposite\nof actionable. Distinct from the obligation columns: a lapsed certification\nis missing now but was filed once, and the two need different letters.\n\n`update-client` finally ran against the live API, so the generated client\ncarries the export endpoints and every filter added since. Three things\nfollow: the hand-written `zExportReportsQuery` extension is deleted as its\nown comment instructed; the register''s employee-count filter becomes a\nmulti-select, which is what widening that param was for; and the data-export\nscreen stops sending only the first selected bucket.","tree":{"sha":"c234656a09309c14ef8d428cd1312446d5d25308","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/c234656a09309c14ef8d428cd1312446d5d25308"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGIyZmYyYTgyZTIwMjFmYWUzYWY5Nzg3Y2M0MTIxNjhhODJmYzY1YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d","sha":"da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d"}],"sha":"b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/b2ff2a82e2021fae3af9787cc412168a82fc65a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:14:29Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"fix(doe): declare the access policy on the export endpoints\n\nBoth export routes were refused with 403 \"This endpoint declares no access\npolicy\". `DeclaredAccessGuard` default-denies any route whose `@UseGuards`\nchain does not name BOTH a verified token and an identity guard, and the\ncontroller declared only `TokenJwtAuthGuard`.\n\nThe failure reached the admin as \"download interrupted\", because the browser\nwas navigating rather than fetching: the proxy passed the 403 straight\nthrough and Chrome reported the transfer instead of the cause.\n\n`swagger-coverage.spec.ts` already asserts this for every routed handler and\nnamed both handlers by name. It did not catch the regression before it\nshipped because only the `doe-modules` suite was run — the controller lives\nin the API app, whose suite was never run against the change.\n\nAlso logs the upstream status and body when a proxied export fails. A failed\ndownload shows no body and leaves nothing in the page console, so without\nthis the only signal is the browser''s own wording, which describes the\ntransfer and not the reason.","tree":{"sha":"07fb6f174f8462e673a527069e743dbf5d864aa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/07fb6f174f8462e673a527069e743dbf5d864aa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGRhMDQwZWVlZmFjNDE2ZmI0Yjk4MGY3OTFiNjJiN2Q3NGQwMWNkM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb","sha":"e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb"}],"sha":"da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/da040eeefac416fb4b980f791b62b7d74d01cd3d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:01:59Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"feat(doe): wire the Skýrslur dataset into \"Keyra út lista\"\n\nThe screen shipped with the dataset toggle rendered but only Fyrirtæki\nworking. This fills in the other half: filter panel, results preview and\nexport, all driven by the same submit gate.\n\n`reportsRouter.list` takes a hand-written extension of the generated query\nschema. The dimensions it adds all exist on `GetReportsQueryDto` today — the\ngenerated client lags because it is rebuilt from a RUNNING API, not from the\nDTOs. The extension carries a note to delete it once the client is next\nregenerated, since a hand-written schema that outlives its reason is how the\ntwo drift. It also repeats the warning from `companyRouter`: an input key the\nschema does not name is stripped silently, so a filter added to the panel and\nnot to the schema appears to do nothing, with no error anywhere.\n\n`ReportExportFilter` is a sibling of `CompanyFilter` rather than a reuse. The\ntwo share a company card, but a report also has a type, a status, a\ncommunication state and four date ranges, and the shared half is three\ncontrols — folding both into one component would mean a prop per control on\nboth screens. The controls they DO share are imported as they are, so\n\"Sveitarfélög\" means the same thing on both datasets.\n\nTwo things the type filter deliberately does not offer. `IMPROVEMENT_PLAN`,\nwhich the vinnslusvæði shows as a third pseudo-type: an úrbótaáætlun is a\nstate OF a skýrslugjöf, not a kind of filing, and the export carries it as\nits own column. And DRAFT among the statuses: the server filters drafts out\nof the requested set even when a status filter names them, so offering it\nwould be a control that silently does nothing.\n\nEmployee count is a multi-select here, unlike the register''s single-select —\nthe report query takes a list, and \"25–49 and 50+\" is the question this\ndataset exists to answer.\n\nThe preview table is six columns against the file''s thirty-eight. It is there\nto confirm the filter caught the right reports before downloading, not to be\nthe file; rows link through so an admin who spots something odd can go and\nlook at it.","tree":{"sha":"0a8fe3f33942c1b193f53d49a9d35b66b7a38999","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/0a8fe3f33942c1b193f53d49a9d35b66b7a38999"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGU1MGU4MTY4NDU0NmE3YWJkZjRhZjY3ZDgyOTRkNmI1ODExZThhZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07","sha":"2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07"}],"sha":"e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/e50e81684546a7abdf4af67d8294d6b5811e8afb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:55:24Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"feat(doe): add the \"Keyra út lista\" screen and wire the front-page panel\n\nThe front page has shipped an ImagePanel titled \"Keyra út lista\" with\n`link=\"#\"` since the design landed. This gives it somewhere to go.\n\nNew route `/gagnautdrattur`, added to `NAV_PATHS` — which both adds the nav\nentry and gates the page, so one entry is the whole registration. Not\nadmin-only: the data is already reachable through Fyrirtæki and\nVinnslusvæði, and this only reshapes it.\n\nThe screen deliberately does NOT query as you type, unlike the register and\nthe vinnslusvæði. Nothing is fetched until \"Sækja lista\" is pressed, because\nthe point of the page is to narrow a large list before asking for it, and a\ntable that reshuffles under every keystroke invites exporting the wrong\nthing. `submitted` holds that snapshot, and BOTH the table and the export\nlink are built from it — editing the panel afterwards changes neither until\nthe button is pressed again.\n\nBecause the results appear in response to a button rather than to typing,\nthe results region takes focus after a fetch and carries `aria-live`, so the\nchange reaches keyboard and screen-reader users and not only sighted ones.\n\n`CompanyFilter`, `CompanyTable`, `SelectFilter` and the option maps are\nreused as they are rather than forked — the filter panel on this screen has\nto mean exactly what the same panel means on the register.\n\nThe export link carries the submitted filter with NO paging, so the file is\nthe whole matching set rather than the page on screen, plus a `filterSummary`\nbuilt from the labels the admin actually saw. That is what the workbook''s\n\"Um útdráttinn\" sheet records: the server has codes, this side has the\nwords. `api/export/[dataset]` proxies to the bearer-guarded endpoint the same\nway `api/salary-template` already does, since an `<a href>` carries no token.\n\nThe Skýrslur dataset renders its toggle but still needs the report filters\nregenerated into the client before it can be wired; the Fyrirtæki dataset\nworks end to end.","tree":{"sha":"3ea2c6fe41fa6796e5109453135ccd667fb01613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/3ea2c6fe41fa6796e5109453135ccd667fb01613"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDJiMzM4OTM4Yjk4NmVkNzRmZDg1M2M2YTc3YWQyOTBlOTFjMmFmMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e","sha":"cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e"}],"sha":"2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/2b338938b986ed74fd853c6a77ad290e91c2af07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:49:04Z","email":"disa@hugsmidjan.is","name":"disaerna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:08:22Z","email":"disa.erna@gmail.com","name":"Ásdís Erna Guðmundsdóttir"},"message":"feat(doe): add the data-export API behind \"Keyra út lista\"\n\nThe admin UI can filter the register and the reports but cannot get either\nout of the browser, so the Directorate''s published figures are still\nassembled by hand. This is the API half: two endpoints that take the SAME\nquery DTO as the list they mirror and return the whole filtered set as a\nfile.\n\n`GET /api/v1/export/companies` and `/export/reports`, xlsx by default and\ncsv on request. Both resolve their filter through the list''s own `where`\nbuilder rather than a second query — an export that resolved a filter even\nslightly differently from the screen it was launched from would be wrong in\nthe worst way: plausible, and only checkable by counting rows by hand.\n`buildReportListWhere` moved out of `ReportService` for exactly that reason,\nand `findAllByFilter` mirrors the existing `findMailRecipientsByFilter`.\n\nFilters added, all needed to reproduce the published dashboard:\n\n- `employeeCountCategory` is now a list. It took one value, so \"everyone the\n  law reaches\" — 25–49 AND 50+ — was unaskable. A bare value still parses.\n- The report list gained the company dimensions it had none of: size,\n  sector, ÍSAT category/section, region, postcode, plus salary-data period,\n  communication status and equality source. These resolve through one\n  correlated EXISTS against the parent `company_report` snapshot, so a group\n  filing cannot multiply into a row per subsidiary.\n\nTwo things the old register modelled that this deliberately does not: the\nvottun/staðfesting split and the gildistímabil counter. The taxonomy here is\nthe two filings a company makes — jafnréttisáætlun and skýrslugjöf — and\ncarrying the retired shapes forward would preserve them past their purpose.\n\nAll five sectors stay separate rather than folding Ráðuneyti and Ríkisaðilar\ninto one \"ríkið\" bucket to match the three the dashboard shows. A reader can\nsum two columns; nobody can split one back apart.\n\nHeadcount needs no new column: `report.average_employee_*_count` is real\nsubmitted data, so the company export reads it off the most recent APPROVED\nreport. Approved only — a submitted report is a claim, not a fact.\n\nEach workbook carries an \"Um útdráttinn\" sheet naming the filter, the\ntimestamp and the row count. These files get mailed on and quoted months\nlater, and one with no record of the filter behind it cannot be reproduced.","tree":{"sha":"105a4ff5ea0624f67f76f13ebef82cc64eee8701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/105a4ff5ea0624f67f76f13ebef82cc64eee8701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19873770?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/disaerna","id":19873770,"login":"disaerna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODczNzcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/disaerna","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGNlYzAyNjI2NmVhZjIzMzlkNmM0MjVhYTg3NGE5Y2VkNTEyMjY3NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76","sha":"212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76"}],"sha":"cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/cec026266eaf2339d6c425aa874a9ced5122674e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24840451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:08:43Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:08:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doe): show how a company''s employee count changes between submissions (#1563)\n\n* feat(doe): expose a company''s employee count history\n\nGET /api/v1/reports/company/:companyId/employee-count-history returns the\naverage headcount by gender, the total, and the size bracket from the\nsubmission snapshot for each report the company filed itself, newest first.\n\nExcluded: drafts, withdrawn predecessors of a resubmission, filings with no\ncounts, and group reports the company was only a subsidiary on, since those\ncounts describe the whole group. Ties on createdAt break by id so the order\nis stable.\n\n* feat(doe): show how a company''s employee count changes between submissions\n\nThe report''s Fyrirtækið tab adds a Samtals figure, shows the change on each\nfigure since the company''s previous submission, names that submission, and\nlinks to the company page''s Starfsmannafjöldasaga.\n\nThat section on the company''s Upplýsingar tab lists every submission''s\ncounts and size bracket. It is hidden when there is nothing to list, and it\nopens and scrolls into view when reached through the link.\n\n* fix(doe): date employee count history by submission, not draft open\n\nReview follow-ups on the employee count history.\n\n- submittedAt and the ordering now come from the company_report snapshot,\n  which is written at submit on every channel. A portal report''s own\n  created_at is when its draft was opened, so history order and the report\n  tab''s \"previous\" could be wrong.\n- The report tab takes the previous entry by position in the server''s list,\n  so it always matches the company page, same-instant filings included. A\n  failed history load now says so instead of silently dropping the deltas.\n- Entries carry includesImprovementPlan, and one reportTypeLabel helper names\n  a report the same way on the history, the report tab and the reports tab.\n- The spec pins the selected attributes and covers the empty and\n  improvement-plan cases.\n- The history anchor moves to lib/constants, and the docs say \"withdrawn\"\n  rather than only resubmission predecessors.","tree":{"sha":"9a8c0fc09ad65e4c05372623165307b0ef7df069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/9a8c0fc09ad65e4c05372623165307b0ef7df069"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a8c0fc09ad65e4c05372623165307b0ef7df069\nparent 45918d4a6a214ad0adfad5a825a5777ede0eb9af\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1790611723 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790611723 +0000\n\nfeat(doe): show how a company''s employee count changes between submissions (#1563)\n\n* feat(doe): expose a company''s employee count history\n\nGET /api/v1/reports/company/:companyId/employee-count-history returns the\naverage headcount by gender, the total, and the size bracket from the\nsubmission snapshot for each report the company filed itself, newest first.\n\nExcluded: drafts, withdrawn predecessors of a resubmission, filings with no\ncounts, and group reports the company was only a subsidiary on, since those\ncounts describe the whole group. Ties on createdAt break by id so the order\nis stable.\n\n* feat(doe): show how a company''s employee count changes between submissions\n\nThe report''s Fyrirtækið tab adds a Samtals figure, shows the change on each\nfigure since the company''s previous submission, names that submission, and\nlinks to the company page''s Starfsmannafjöldasaga.\n\nThat section on the company''s Upplýsingar tab lists every submission''s\ncounts and size bracket. It is hidden when there is nothing to list, and it\nopens and scrolls into view when reached through the link.\n\n* fix(doe): date employee count history by submission, not draft open\n\nReview follow-ups on the employee count history.\n\n- submittedAt and the ordering now come from the company_report snapshot,\n  which is written at submit on every channel. A portal report''s own\n  created_at is when its draft was opened, so history order and the report\n  tab''s \"previous\" could be wrong.\n- The report tab takes the previous entry by position in the server''s list,\n  so it always matches the company page, same-instant filings included. A\n  failed history load now says so instead of silently dropping the deltas.\n- Entries carry includesImprovementPlan, and one reportTypeLabel helper names\n  a report the same way on the history, the report tab and the reports tab.\n- The spec pins the selected attributes and covers the empty and\n  improvement-plan cases.\n- The history anchor moves to lib/constants, and the docs say \"withdrawn\"\n  rather than only resubmission predecessors.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqupELCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9Z4QAImWe0IApCgDGesMS+SDWZKd\nygPWDN/WPB+OgHE7U9GHXwdDaEFcyxgy3OMFFo760nGz7AqcajXDWU1s/j5x7tHJ\nNqhYmb8lx78NSU16fiu4nbREeEThp1R89eLlMCIPcH68MRBBfK3wgUpnhde+c0sY\nxENNLN5AiD6WyN+yxyC6YreU+/dcK3wHfOsaTExTHjJRiy0nlpxqqg7G545V28Ih\nXgqPjF4esb5JYJUWmaqr/1nMNZ90txBlUz2WVaOun31FW70vZg2OCF9A/puB4Q7/\nBjagvP98abV1aM9mad7Cnidvjywe2BnwjjCIlnXDLIH/oIpPZok6Lqu0kVi1mpE9\nEr2WMsDopy7QP/wrF0qTfFF8wG5f0jU4Ta/yBpubCrZBXn10UxOeaF7mJ4jzaEaI\n1eZggGv2EStYthh/M45qCw03CawwtIrPZUx6xw4CWjq0foFxELrbdRZYMIy/FRu7\nCOQ3zKCZgOuRGTHHt6w0yFPBo66gFs9x0aURNT36siiAO1fWzb/lY+hKAKNZ37oZ\nWV5iJEI0hyLCahsZU8D7iCnDmlknaOHhbIObvU9cPpvaSGxRpWrFiLKSLwrbHKqS\nVQrZIIb4foIX3KpJ4vsJxup1THQEkwyGzzHYvCDvc2pJCLQ1ymEeYJYVuCJRZZil\nrlsJ3YJhpBWf/mosi+kK\n=fXoX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T16:08:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDIxMmI4NDNkYjAzZmZhNmQxMDRlNDk0M2QwN2JkYjBjMmMyNmZhNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/45918d4a6a214ad0adfad5a825a5777ede0eb9af","sha":"45918d4a6a214ad0adfad5a825a5777ede0eb9af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/45918d4a6a214ad0adfad5a825a5777ede0eb9af"}],"sha":"212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/212b843db03ffa6d104e4943d07bdb0c2c26fa76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/45918d4a6a214ad0adfad5a825a5777ede0eb9af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:09:21Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:09:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(lg): close same-day publishing at noon (#1562)\n\n* test(lg): give the schemas lib a jest target\n\nMirrors libs/legal-gazette/html: bare @swc/jest, a spec tsconfig, and the\nspec files excluded from the lib build.\n\n* fix(lg): close same-day publishing at noon\n\nSkiptalok adverts submitted in the evening were booked for the same day.\nThe noon cutoff only existed in a client helper, and nothing enforced it:\n\n- getNextValidPublishingDate only applies the noon rule when its input is\n  today. The Skiptalok form fed it a historical minDate, which came back\n  unchanged, so the picker offered today at any hour.\n- addDivisionEnding passed scheduledAt straight to createAdvert.\n- validateFuture only required \"after midnight today\", so a default date\n  picked in the morning still passed on an evening submit.\n\nThe cutoff now lives in the schemas lib and reads both the hour and the\nday in Reykjavik time (UTC), the same day the publishing task buckets\nscheduledAt into. validateFuture and the Skiptalok input use it, and\naddDivisionEnding rejects a same-day date after noon with a 400. The\nSkiptalok picker clamps its minDate with a new getEarliestPublishingDate.\n\n* fix(lg): address review on the noon cutoff\n\nSend publish dates as the picked calendar day. #1490 made every pure-date\npicker send toCalendarDateIso, but PublishingFields overwrote the\ncontroller''s snapped value with toISOString(), and the Skiptalok and\nRitstjórn pickers never snapped at all. From a browser east of UTC a\npicked day arrived as the previous day: the new cutoff rejected a valid\nnext-day pick after noon, and before this change the same pick published\na day early. getEarliestPublishingDate now reads the cutoff at Reykjavik\nnoon rather than browser-local noon.\n\nExempt editors. The Ritstjórn create modals validate with the same\nrefined answers schemas, so every afternoon their own default failed.\nThe cutoff is an intake rule for applicants; the admin inputs now use\neditor variants that keep every other rule and still reject past days.\n\nApply the cutoff to Skiptafundur. addDivisionMeeting publishes on the\nmeeting date, and CreateDivisionMeeting had the same unclamped minDate\nas the Skiptalok picker. The API check moves into a shared\nassertPublishingDateOpen, and the rejection specs now assert the reason,\nnot just BadRequestException, with the clock pinned so fixtures in the\npast cannot pass for the wrong reason.\n\nAlso drop ''html'' from the schemas jest config and cross-reference the\ntwo copies of the cutoff hour.","tree":{"sha":"14e33b0ba53b0eb4b71b97e8c4cd5572ed1163e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/14e33b0ba53b0eb4b71b97e8c4cd5572ed1163e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/45918d4a6a214ad0adfad5a825a5777ede0eb9af","verification":{"payload":"tree 14e33b0ba53b0eb4b71b97e8c4cd5572ed1163e0\nparent d1430f9de2003d231a97532e711f3446afed9fae\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1790604561 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790604561 +0000\n\nfix(lg): close same-day publishing at noon (#1562)\n\n* test(lg): give the schemas lib a jest target\n\nMirrors libs/legal-gazette/html: bare @swc/jest, a spec tsconfig, and the\nspec files excluded from the lib build.\n\n* fix(lg): close same-day publishing at noon\n\nSkiptalok adverts submitted in the evening were booked for the same day.\nThe noon cutoff only existed in a client helper, and nothing enforced it:\n\n- getNextValidPublishingDate only applies the noon rule when its input is\n  today. The Skiptalok form fed it a historical minDate, which came back\n  unchanged, so the picker offered today at any hour.\n- addDivisionEnding passed scheduledAt straight to createAdvert.\n- validateFuture only required \"after midnight today\", so a default date\n  picked in the morning still passed on an evening submit.\n\nThe cutoff now lives in the schemas lib and reads both the hour and the\nday in Reykjavik time (UTC), the same day the publishing task buckets\nscheduledAt into. validateFuture and the Skiptalok input use it, and\naddDivisionEnding rejects a same-day date after noon with a 400. The\nSkiptalok picker clamps its minDate with a new getEarliestPublishingDate.\n\n* fix(lg): address review on the noon cutoff\n\nSend publish dates as the picked calendar day. #1490 made every pure-date\npicker send toCalendarDateIso, but PublishingFields overwrote the\ncontroller''s snapped value with toISOString(), and the Skiptalok and\nRitstjórn pickers never snapped at all. From a browser east of UTC a\npicked day arrived as the previous day: the new cutoff rejected a valid\nnext-day pick after noon, and before this change the same pick published\na day early. getEarliestPublishingDate now reads the cutoff at Reykjavik\nnoon rather than browser-local noon.\n\nExempt editors. The Ritstjórn create modals validate with the same\nrefined answers schemas, so every afternoon their own default failed.\nThe cutoff is an intake rule for applicants; the admin inputs now use\neditor variants that keep every other rule and still reject past days.\n\nApply the cutoff to Skiptafundur. addDivisionMeeting publishes on the\nmeeting date, and CreateDivisionMeeting had the same unclamped minDate\nas the Skiptalok picker. The API check moves into a shared\nassertPublishingDateOpen, and the rejection specs now assert the reason,\nnot just BadRequestException, with the clock pinned so fixtures in the\npast cannot pass for the wrong reason.\n\nAlso drop ''html'' from the schemas jest config and cross-reference the\ntwo copies of the cutoff hour.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqunURCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASdcQAB43ffCzF2/2wmsuVlnOiTx2\nAgieKYagQEtT/NqzUpKluQetXE+dwGr9d3/QwFvd/I1+87Izna1PavgYd+sYVdy0\nIFe7h+rvoRwknxeB64btrSh/XeUJczNnI8MyLHGDq7gbSAAPncSJwyBebmz2mcCf\nq3rruMUbL9g/ltxl+6Rf/yCSNANBZIDNtue91H6i5ohUIuSGQeuvvoDNlSNsQFmP\nJ2yXYuV9Au0MF1XtQfo+w2TRSjJiF/daTk+jf/cuqWiQbEg1U1iLJPcz+gv8IB7m\nzQwQu6vfywZOx38o7LBPefH4XDfzwo3x9eCo78XYkGSYOLcrFeM1HW5b1d+4UufK\nQC09+5rdtvxCtV+O5bqXu3sl0/3O0UKFKF1aKbm/Ids/l34YSlNOY26qak+EZKvv\noHoM6mbTOIxxeJswYJaLEKqQTwC1AFxtrRvL1tvscWJqPZVkxsDJsp6w+joDjFx9\nZGJnWy84Fez4yY9xRcUIi+u90i0y7RC0LFHJ8WA7dO+K16gejxSa1a3z2qn355Y6\nVNNANhJN0AML9seI/dSnt3wp8pY9Sr5eGb3kKgIsNi0iJSo8cPC+HFytO/k6ncBo\nE57YSqUNlZqQDBsH7NyGorL4BCcXfWCKDJ/+ogr+uZw/qjtVhBWIIFXFaT