g.","tree":{"sha":"b3c9e6b7a485d0942498ae52f17f10afe3c9af52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/b3c9e6b7a485d0942498ae52f17f10afe3c9af52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/ba86fd9869f5d5afe937d87a3ce51eda74b54848","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/ba86fd9869f5d5afe937d87a3ce51eda74b54848","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGJhODZmZDk4NjlmNWQ1YWZlOTM3ZDg3YTNjZTUxZWRhNzRiNTQ4NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a","sha":"c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a"}],"sha":"ba86fd9869f5d5afe937d87a3ce51eda74b54848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/ba86fd9869f5d5afe937d87a3ce51eda74b54848"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:58:52Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:24:58Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"message":"fix(doe): guarantee full firm approval and flag legacy narrow grants\n\nReview of #1554:\n\n- Firm approval takes no scopes: PartnerClientService.create always\n  approves every scope, and m-20260924-partner-client-full-approval widens\n  live firms approved before. So a delegation, which copies the approval,\n  is what the consent screen promises.\n- An empty scope set on a new key is a 400 instead of meaning \"every\n  scope\"; CreateApiKeyDto validates ArrayMinSize/ArrayUnique/IsEnum.\n- Company keys and delegations made before all-or-nothing are not\n  migrated — they are the company''s own grants. partner-web and the admin\n  key tab tag them \"Takmarkaðar heimildir\", with what to do.\n- Guide notes the pre-24-September keys and delegations and points\n  vendors at scopes on GET /partner/delegations; example shows the full\n  set. Stale comments and route descriptions updated; db README records\n  the invariant and the migration.","tree":{"sha":"dfd5c68498e511fa10fa7a6a3598a447d01398ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/dfd5c68498e511fa10fa7a6a3598a447d01398ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGMwNWRlMWVmMmQyYzVhZGEzNmNlZjZjYzA2ZTVkN2E5YTEwNGMzN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e","sha":"90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e"}],"sha":"c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/c05de1ef2d2c5ada36cef6cc06e5d7a9a104c37a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:04:50Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:24:58Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"message":"feat(doe): make vendor and key access all or nothing\n\nScope-by-scope choices confused employers and reviewers who rarely handle\nAPI keys, and a key that could file but not author the starfsmat would\nhave landed on Jafnréttisstofa to untangle.\n\nDEFAULT_API_KEY_SCOPES is now every scope, scoring:write included. A grant\nwith no scopes hands over the firm''s whole approval. No screen offers a\nscope choice: doe-web''s vendor approval and company key modals, and\npartner-web''s consent form and company key modal, send none. The API still\naccepts and enforces an explicit subset. PartnerProviderDto.scopes, added\nonly to feed the consent checkboxes, is removed again.","tree":{"sha":"c3cb8deef2728b6c9df8e3a3ce698e211686588e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/c3cb8deef2728b6c9df8e3a3ce698e211686588e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDkwNTk0ZWYwMGRhZTlhNGIwYWZiZjE2MWQ1YzNjNTE4NWMwZjE3MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983","sha":"418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983"}],"sha":"90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/90594ef00dae9a4b0afbf161d5c3c5185c0f171e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:38:57Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:17:02Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"message":"fix(doe): expire auth cookies with Secure and pin the cookie-name plumbing\n\nReview of #1553:\n\n- access-denied expired its cookies with a bare delete, which sends no\n  Secure attribute; browsers reject that for __Secure-/__Host- names, so\n  in production nothing was cleared. It now expires them through\n  expiredAuthCookieOptions().\n- Specs pin that getToken gets the cookie name in logout and\n  revoke-refresh, and that createAuthMiddleware passes cookies to withAuth\n  for a prefix and none without one.\n- An empty prefix counts as none in sessionCookieName, matching the\n  middleware. The spec restores env keys individually.","tree":{"sha":"a91c4c06a5c2e9617cc78d13a0ec5a01acee31e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/a91c4c06a5c2e9617cc78d13a0ec5a01acee31e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDQxOGRhNDY1Njc3Nzk2MWQ5Y2ZiNzFkZDc5Y2VkYjhkNDM5NjE5ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787","sha":"13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787"}],"sha":"418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/418da4656777961d9cfb71dd79cedb8d43961983"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T11:43:57Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:17:02Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"message":"fix(doe): give each DoE web its own NextAuth cookie names\n\ndoe-web and partner-web both kept their session in next-auth.session-token.\nCookies are scoped by host, not port, so on localhost signing in to one\noverwrote the other''s session, which then failed to decrypt under the other\napp''s NEXTAUTH_SECRET and read as a logout. partner-web''s access-denied\nroute also cleared every next-auth.* cookie, doe-web''s included.\n\n@dmr.is/auth gains sessionCookies.ts (appAuthCookies, sessionCookieName,\nisAppAuthCookie); the refresh middleware, logout and revoke-refresh handlers\ntake the cookie name. Apps that pass no prefix keep NextAuth''s defaults.","tree":{"sha":"99ca7b3f6209382dc57de81810e09daaf115c2e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/99ca7b3f6209382dc57de81810e09daaf115c2e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDEzYjU2ZjZlOWJmNjQ3N2ViYmU0YjdhODU2NTI3YjI2YjkwYTc3ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/4a31c6c612342e4efd6f36286510e23f776a3d3a","sha":"4a31c6c612342e4efd6f36286510e23f776a3d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/4a31c6c612342e4efd6f36286510e23f776a3d3a"}],"sha":"13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/13b56f6e9bf6477ebbe4b7a856527b26b90a7787"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/4a31c6c612342e4efd6f36286510e23f776a3d3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:12:57Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:12:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): fail prod deploys that roll back or never stabilise (#1549)\n\n* fix(shared): fail prod deploys that roll back or never stabilise\n\nThe DoE deploy returned as soon as terragrunt registered the task\ndefinition, and the Útgáfa wait passed on a rollback: the circuit breaker\nrestores the old task definition and the service then reports stable.\n\nBoth deploys now go through a wait-for-services action that waits for\nsteady state and then checks that each service''s primary deployment runs\nan image tagged with the release version. The DoE wait runs after the\ninfrastructure commit, as Útgáfa''s does, and the deploy job''s existing\n`if` keeps a red DoE job from blocking Útgáfa.\n\n* fix(shared): poll rollouts to COMPLETED instead of trusting the waiter\n\n`services-stable` passes once runningCount matches desiredCount, which\ncounts tasks the load balancer has not health-checked yet, while the\ncircuit breaker stays armed until the deployment is COMPLETED. A deploy\ncould go green and then roll back. The waiter also takes at most 10\nservices and gives up after 10 minutes, and any AWS error aborted the\ncheck with no message.\n\nwait-for-services now polls describe-services itself, in batches of 10,\nfor up to TIMEOUT_MINUTES (default 20). A service passes once its primary\ndeployment runs the release tag, is COMPLETED and is the only deployment.\nIt is reported separately as rolled back, failed to roll out, missing,\nstill rolling out, or uncheckable after five AWS errors in a row.\n\nAlso documents on on-release that re-running an old release''s DoE deploy\nre-runs the Útgáfa deploy at the old tag without approval.\n\n* fix(shared): count failed polls, not failed calls, when waiting on ECS\n\nThe give-up limit counted failed AWS calls and reset on any successful\ndescribe-services. So it depended on the number of services: a persistent\ndescribe-task-definition failure on DoE''s two services never reached it\nand ran to the deadline, while a brief blip across Útgáfa''s nine gave up\non the first poll. It now counts polls in which any call failed.\n\nAlso:\n- a previous-revision primary is a rollback only from the second poll,\n  since describe-services is eventually consistent after the update\n- a whitespace-only SERVICES fails instead of passing unchecked\n- passing without a rolloutState is warned about, and documented\n- the header no longer claims a different tag is the only rollback signal\n- test/run.sh drives the script against a fake aws\n\n* fix(shared): point the DoE wait''s partner TODO at the dev-only rollout\n\n* fix(shared): run the rollout waits as jobs nothing depends on\n\nThe DoE wait ran inside deploy-jafnrettisstofa, which the Útgáfa deploy\nneeds for push ordering. So every Útgáfa release waited out DoE''s rollout,\nand a red DoE wait invited a re-run that also redeployed Útgáfa without\napproval.\n\nBoth deploy actions now end at their infrastructure commit, and each\nproduct gets a wait job that needs only its own deploy. The push order is\nunchanged. Re-running a red wait now only re-checks the rollout.\nwait-for-services configures its own AWS credentials for this, and the\nÚtgáfa action drops the SERVICES input it only used for the old wait.\n\ndeploy-to-prod.yml gets the same two jobs so it keeps waiting at all.\n\n* ci(shared): run the wait-for-services harness in the quality pipeline","tree":{"sha":"cc5af6b6c76d6696bc9932ec91df3542fdc988df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/cc5af6b6c76d6696bc9932ec91df3542fdc988df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/4a31c6c612342e4efd6f36286510e23f776a3d3a","verification":{"payload":"tree cc5af6b6c76d6696bc9932ec91df3542fdc988df\nparent 28ecf5fe5e5489110938d71941f40cbfc4f04f0d\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1790266377 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790266377 +0000\n\nfix(shared): fail prod deploys that roll back or never stabilise (#1549)\n\n* fix(shared): fail prod deploys that roll back or never stabilise\n\nThe DoE deploy returned as soon as terragrunt registered the task\ndefinition, and the Útgáfa wait passed on a rollback: the circuit breaker\nrestores the old task definition and the service then reports stable.\n\nBoth deploys now go through a wait-for-services action that waits for\nsteady state and then checks that each service''s primary deployment runs\nan image tagged with the release version. The DoE wait runs after the\ninfrastructure commit, as Útgáfa''s does, and the deploy job''s existing\n`if` keeps a red DoE job from blocking Útgáfa.\n\n* fix(shared): poll rollouts to COMPLETED instead of trusting the waiter\n\n`services-stable` passes once runningCount matches desiredCount, which\ncounts tasks the load balancer has not health-checked yet, while the\ncircuit breaker stays armed until the deployment is COMPLETED. A deploy\ncould go green and then roll back. The waiter also takes at most 10\nservices and gives up after 10 minutes, and any AWS error aborted the\ncheck with no message.\n\nwait-for-services now polls describe-services itself, in batches of 10,\nfor up to TIMEOUT_MINUTES (default 20). A service passes once its primary\ndeployment runs the release tag, is COMPLETED and is the only deployment.\nIt is reported separately as rolled back, failed to roll out, missing,\nstill rolling out, or uncheckable after five AWS errors in a row.\n\nAlso documents on on-release that re-running an old release''s DoE deploy\nre-runs the Útgáfa deploy at the old tag without approval.\n\n* fix(shared): count failed polls, not failed calls, when waiting on ECS\n\nThe give-up limit counted failed AWS calls and reset on any successful\ndescribe-services. So it depended on the number of services: a persistent\ndescribe-task-definition failure on DoE''s two services never reached it\nand ran to the deadline, while a brief blip across Útgáfa''s nine gave up\non the first poll. It now counts polls in which any call failed.\n\nAlso:\n- a previous-revision primary is a rollback only from the second poll,\n  since describe-services is eventually consistent after the update\n- a whitespace-only SERVICES fails instead of passing unchecked\n- passing without a rolloutState is warned about, and documented\n- the header no longer claims a different tag is the only rollback signal\n- test/run.sh drives the script against a fake aws\n\n* fix(shared): point the DoE wait''s partner TODO at the dev-only rollout\n\n* fix(shared): run the rollout waits as jobs nothing depends on\n\nThe DoE wait ran inside deploy-jafnrettisstofa, which the Útgáfa deploy\nneeds for push ordering. So every Útgáfa release waited out DoE''s rollout,\nand a red DoE wait invited a re-run that also redeployed Útgáfa without\napproval.\n\nBoth deploy actions now end at their infrastructure commit, and each\nproduct gets a wait job that needs only its own deploy. The push order is\nunchanged. Re-running a red wait now only re-checks the rollout.\nwait-for-services configures its own AWS credentials for this, and the\nÚtgáfa action drops the SERVICES input it only used for the old wait.\n\ndeploy-to-prod.yml gets the same two jobs so it keeps waiting at all.\n\n* ci(shared): run the wait-for-services harness in the quality pipeline","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtUwJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPGIQADWEbmNDGIB/41LvdU01pXAZ\nplXEIOy4L71lEm7y2+P0JJK46z3Tix2JZxajd8FrUq07pcCG4Yk47F/wih6c8zoF\nQFUsYEa9/v4hw3TGeKfYgwoV1DohbJPtN3LhAMFZl7x0m7aZkdZVCMWg3TVjZwOH\npkubAnb+thUuNC4zc54NCKx1sd3vRM/tLoBPFcoXB8ly8Y9JK3Hj77eCOscGEDXe\nHXXWpK/WVLE6/5Se/14ULr2t7IPSwAbBYQmleKw8kGx799sb/xVbqtcFRE7bXRC2\nEm66IopeLWP39yr6LAzuXNfpf9ywJzA49eJtIT1z1iQzkLBhvwORC7IbLkSgBB1g\nXlASTmdqVDQVzYPUX1Dcz4ihbQeYfpRFbAqD2V014mrYt0fkvZoo5vNcTuD6tWcY\nt6p0RLJditXecmZouSy/qgHI583CBxEmo2QxbGwA8xh9wtzVvVE9Y2EG6qvRLwzl\nxyq97tC4CHcC3Zyl0zYBj22DMTu8gkaZt3rUPJWqn3hZA0GHS8LqOMHfO18nuyQP\nVGYeXieAnOwLZ549vQz2ik157QIwES5/Bd1gmXG/pvjaeiueMwm8IVzD70C5zTfZ\nPhslxjYYVmdCLT1Q+h9P/lIM+kpwSa7ZUEWtjAlrSrfI+IhZOZwqjlzMy0N+qt9J\n26rGUFWXxZ6j8Mw/t2G9\n=rkwM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T16:12:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":fa