s://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/f9749494ab78ed5c88fcb839ecd35db3aeef04cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:29:30Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:29:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(lg): fill in publication number on published aukatilkynningar (#1548)\n\n* fix(lg): fill in publication number on published aukatilkynningar\n\nAdditional announcements write \"(Reiknast við útgáfu)-NNN\" into the advert\ncontent at creation, before a publication number exists, and nothing replaced\nit at publish, so the placeholder reached publishedHtml and the PDF. Resolve it\nat render time.\n\nThe publishing task also rendered HTML before assigning the publication\nnumber, so a first publication through it showed the placeholder as its serial.\n\n* refactor(lg): keep the pending publication number in core/constants\n\nThe company utils were importing the render module, and through it the\nSequelize model graph, for one string.","tree":{"sha":"a7d6e1462b54a35a38fe9fa02d4124c0f84c1b64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/a7d6e1462b54a35a38fe9fa02d4124c0f84c1b64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/f9749494ab78ed5c88fcb839ecd35db3aeef04cd","verification":{"payload":"tree a7d6e1462b54a35a38fe9fa02d4124c0f84c1b64\nparent 7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5\nauthor Jón Bjarni Ólafsson <dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com> 1790173770 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790173770 +0000\n\nfix(lg): fill in publication number on published aukatilkynningar (#1548)\n\n* fix(lg): fill in publication number on published aukatilkynningar\n\nAdditional announcements write \"(Reiknast við útgáfu)-NNN\" into the advert\ncontent at creation, before a publication number exists, and nothing replaced\nit at publish, so the placeholder reached publishedHtml and the PDF. Resolve it\nat render time.\n\nThe publishing task also rendered HTML before assigning the publication\nnumber, so a first publication through it showed the placeholder as its serial.\n\n* refactor(lg): keep the pending publication number in core/constants\n\nThe company utils were importing the render module, and through it the\nSequelize model graph, for one string.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+JKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqNMQAKajX1y1yBK30aTLZII8ceb6\nYgvFEMq5lvt4hlAEflIpfIkJJwFrNgWiUSUhHYg8KneD+fyPUL5OLB/sck5PXzXC\nVboYgRpOWCvXpn/oY3YxllnPhR4DuuFatIBFkOxdXExmnpOHNJVaMR6y2EH3xbw+\nIUCZC+eWYDYglqGic7y993dlRkeGG+i2a+9LUMGE4OReNDhuAXUAUODSKmpExh65\nqlRMztsv1bHuAoIF2U/zUYuHevvHDtZZkMM5Cl+VdGRPDHuBuIYX1goZgF8qpbVi\nn90sbslnr9ITJdib8VrfSL3cdqtIEh9C0liZnhvSNjjKim4FG+JC30wuROj851vo\nJTKzbuwUUwbHpPcrgf194bP3p1gOSE8AedvMfZB3ecJXLe97W7+5+1sx9mWuR3TI\nEK6vtMINlx9F+1HS9dGCs4ifmOMM798ThWr6F0Yj+kPoF+slQkSRuUVWATUHrAmg\nsmEk34y57cPgligFw5fSgwzj+zAubGZUKC5IV2pqNXxbyCbMLLDIgMXyLnSK4YlN\ndOiTga1JT+uE8LkrvPx/XdRCSvB5q8i63r3PX8io0Z3Q5ww6YMPPig5w62edBP4q\n2gjJs3GZ0wh+uyLdkPkl3KPEdwGlLlpKrH6NUQuwRTl7f1Z57RF3hyE60sNkKS37\nGQH6lvXJvfhF6OEXNNnD\n=PHRO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T14:29:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/f9749494ab78ed5c88fcb839ecd35db3aeef04cd","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGY5NzQ5NDk0YWI3OGVkNWM4OGZjYjgzOWVjZDM1ZGIzYWVlZjA0Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5","sha":"7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5"}],"sha":"f9749494ab78ed5c88fcb839ecd35db3aeef04cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/f9749494ab78ed5c88fcb839ecd35db3aeef04cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24840451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:16:44Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:16:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(doe): record the partner channel''s outlier and sibling policy (#1541)\n\n* docs(doe): record the partner channel''s outlier and sibling policy\n\n#1538 and #1539 changed how the partner API postpones outliers and\nreplaces siblings, and the db README still described island.is''s rules\nas the only ones. Docs only.\n\n- Sibling policy: a POSTPONED sibling 409s on island.is but is withdrawn\n  and replaced on the partner API (`withdrawPostponedSibling`), unless it\n  was filed on island.is. Also names the function that does it:\n  `withdrawInflightSibling()`, not `withdrawOrRejectInflightSibling()`.\n- Postponement: no longer only an opt-in. The partner API postpones\n  automatically when outliers are detected and no groups are sent\n  (`postponeUnexplainedOutliers`), and has its own exit route,\n  `PUT /partner/reports/:providerId/outliers`.\n- The submit-side guard is now `resolveOutlierPostponement()` with three\n  cases, and the partner analysis route is an optional dry run rather\n  than a step before submit.\n\n* docs(doe): name the real outlier detection, and scope the outliers PUT\n\nReview round on #1541.\n\n- The preview and submit bullets named `detectOutliers`, which no longer\n  exists; the ±band model it described was replaced by the wage-gap\n  decomposition. They now name `analyzeSalaryPayload()` and\n  `computeDetectedOutlierOrdinals()`, and describe the lágmarksmengi.\n- \"Resolves it later on either channel\" overstated it: each channel''s\n  `PUT …/outliers` only finds its own reports\n  (`findOwnedReportByProviderTuple`). Said so here and in the\n  `report_outlier_group` section.\n- Replay: `status` is the earlier report''s current status and\n  `unexplainedOutlierOrdinals` is absent, with the GET that recovers it.\n- The admin create flow also sets `outliersPostponed`.\n- Two code comments pointed at `CreateReportDto` for options that live on\n  `CreateSalaryOptions`.\n\n* docs(doe): admin-postponed reports have no resolve route\n\nThe channel-scoping sentence added last round did not hold for admin\nfilings: they are SYSTEM reports, and neither outliers PUT can find them,\nso a reviewer can only deny one. Say so. The code gap itself is out of\nscope here.","tree":{"sha":"7591879d96e10260162b25c96ae7c9f21312a85e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/7591879d96e10260162b25c96ae7c9f21312a85e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7591879d96e10260162b25c96ae7c9f21312a85e\nparent 056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1790169404 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790169404 +0000\n\ndocs(doe): record the partner channel''s outlier and sibling policy (#1541)\n\n* docs(doe): record the partner channel''s outlier and sibling policy\n\n#1538 and #1539 changed how the partner API postpones outliers and\nreplaces siblings, and the db README still described island.is''s rules\nas the only ones. Docs only.\n\n- Sibling policy: a POSTPONED sibling 409s on island.is but is withdrawn\n  and replaced on the partner API (`withdrawPostponedSibling`), unless it\n  was filed on island.is. Also names the function that does it:\n  `withdrawInflightSibling()`, not `withdrawOrRejectInflightSibling()`.\n- Postponement: no longer only an opt-in. The partner API postpones\n  automatically when outliers are detected and no groups are sent\n  (`postponeUnexplainedOutliers`), and has its own exit route,\n  `PUT /partner/reports/:providerId/outliers`.\n- The submit-side guard is now `resolveOutlierPostponement()` with three\n  cases, and the partner analysis route is an optional dry run rather\n  than a step before submit.\n\n* docs(doe): name the real outlier detection, and scope the outliers PUT\n\nReview round on #1541.\n\n- The preview and submit bullets named `detectOutliers`, which no longer\n  exists; the ±band model it described was replaced by the wage-gap\n  decomposition. They now name `analyzeSalaryPayload()` and\n  `computeDetectedOutlierOrdinals()`, and describe the lágmarksmengi.\n- \"Resolves it later on either channel\" overstated it: each channel''s\n  `PUT …/outliers` only finds its own reports\n  (`findOwnedReportByProviderTuple`). Said so here and in the\n  `report_outlier_group` section.\n- Replay: `status` is the earlier report''s current status and\n  `unexplainedOutlierOrdinals` is absent, with the GET that recovers it.\n- The admin create flow also sets `outliersPostponed`.\n- Two code comments pointed at `CreateReportDto` for options that live on\n  `CreateSalaryOptions`.\n\n* docs(doe): admin-postponed reports have no resolve route\n\nThe channel-scoping sentence added last round did not hold for admin\nfilings: they are SYSTEM reports, and neither outliers PUT can find them,\nso a reviewer can only deny one. Say so. The code gap itself is out of\nscope here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9E8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQokQAI015SgLONJvjAzqfhrhJf8w\nUXzoJN98tC2tpsdzS9FcQHbStuoaEhWx1FRua1Qswr5qCMh4+uHD7G6o8M1LmAXN\nG4xDixFGV7zoZtpu/XUc63j0+f9KpLrwlXKHcFQ087awgiIUCLKyGNhYb+uDHMUE\nO65ZXq37UcV22r1Y/trvL93BL/osidmsQhTX3yxs0GLasQw+HLwwVwtyGUJOSBZb\nKJYPcZL87WOrwwCvUbUkKFtLX8SzfRxdP+gg3JKwC79U4Bf3omMC0C28TKbE9bj0\nS9usxi97GpKpNkjfC1fdXypwRR84Q4ktFpY/s/0LfNSUT5hXaheD7SVeVKIf7q6b\nYLxIrL3Y4lncPiEBxeGEIXzuV1/AlUif50MSNditgKriiUNlmdC9UCMeexses7gp\nCAiikByZSiPItqwCrrpFr2S8fGMVYbTWc8xmaJH992cU2b4FyKSVWI3wf2KGeayF\ns8OltI/CSeSvgrSNgCvPWl3cvv8QYVjOgKI5Xq9q5a5RW6THQXzSvNKdLuPj8kw3\netFaSW3m4jW59iBBNew+cfl+zCJ2IoozZQYwezeJRkzpzqK/2uzbUa82TtHURMPh\nu84tfUBAqd9UZ9K4UmeTR0D/Kv51w+CuyOXd3UlOtS/wn9di2w8YKWaGGONVRKyX\nWF4y2QWj2Xme2Yd2fg+s\n=yf/K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:16:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDdmZDYwYTFmOTUxMGI1N2YxZWZlNGNmYWE4MzIwZTZiYjFiNjU5YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb","sha":"056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb"}],"sha":"7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/7fd60a1f9510b57f1efe4cfaa8320e6bb1b659b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24840451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:11:55Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:11:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doe): drop the salary renewal window (#1540)\n\n* feat(doe): drop the salary renewal window\n\nA company may now file a salary report whenever it likes. The rule that\nrefused a submission while the current report was due more than six months\nout is removed entirely — no toggle, no env flag — at the project owners''\nrequest (22 Sept 2026).\n\nThe remaining refusals are unchanged: a 404 when nothing covers the\ncompany''s equality obligation, and a 409 when a sibling salary report is\nIN_REVIEW or POSTPONED. Those duplicate guards are what stop runaway\nrefiling now that timing no longer does.\n\n**The eligibility endpoint reports what filing early costs.** The 3-year\nterm still runs from the approval date, so time left on the current\ncertificate is forfeited rather than carried over. `earliestNewDueAt` —\nthe deadline a report filed now would earn if approved today — sits\nbeside `dueAt`, and is returned whether or not the company is eligible.\n`RENEWAL_WINDOW_NOT_OPEN` and `earliestSubmissionDate` are gone; `reason`\nhas one member left, `MISSING_EQUALITY_REPORT`.\n\n**One definition of the 3-year term.** `computeReportValidUntil` is lifted\nout of `approve()` so the date the endpoint quotes cannot drift from the\none approval writes. It uses `setUTCFullYear` where the inline code used\nthe local variant, making `day-boundaries.ts` consistent with its own\nrule. Iceland is UTC, so behaviour is unchanged.\n\nThe gate was only ever enforced behind `API_ENV === ''prod''`, while the\neligibility route evaluated it everywhere — the two disagreed outside\nproduction all along. No migration: `next_salary_report_due_at` keeps\nevery other reader (overdue, reminders, register status, expiry filters).\n\n* fix(doe): address review on the renewal-window removal\n\n- One `REPORT_VALIDITY_YEARS`. `day-boundaries.ts` had declared a second\n  one beside the `constants.ts` copy that `remedy-date.ts` uses, so the\n  validity term and the remedy cap had two sources. It now imports the\n  existing constant, whose warning about the inline copy in `approve()` is\n  resolved.\n- `approve()` still said the next-due date is what the renewal-window\n  check reads. It now names the readers that remain.\n- The partner 409 lists (guide §B7, the status table, the submit route''s\n  description, `PartnerResponse`) left out the cross-type `providerId`\n  conflict, which is reachable here. The status table also contradicted\n  §B7 on island.is-filed POSTPONED siblings.\n- `submitSalary`''s comment said the early-filing cost is \"shown to the\n  applicant\". Nothing shows it yet; it is reported so the portal can.\n- \"It never does\" (guide §B2) and \"never true\" (db README) now say what\n  they rest on: approval-set deadlines, and the launch cohort''s seeded\n  dates, all inside three years.\n- The `day-boundaries.ts` header no longer cites the portal''s \"frá og með\"\n  display, which was `earliestSubmissionDate`.\n\n* docs(doe): finish the 409 lists and the deadline premise\n\nSecond review round.\n\n- The cross-type `providerId` 409 is symmetric: `createEquality` runs the\n  same check, so the equality route''s lists (guide A3, the route''s OpenAPI\n  description) now name it too, matching the salary side and the status\n  table.\n- Guide §B2 stated \"`dueAt` is three years from some past approval\" as a\n  general fact and hedged afterwards. For a deadline carried over from the\n  old register it is data, not a rule, so the approval case comes first\n  and the launch-data bound is stated as what it is.\n- `submitSalary`''s comment had a broken wrap and left out the tuple 409.\n\n* docs(doe): say \"never earlier\", and count the equality conflicts as B6 does\n\nThird review round, wording only.\n\n- \"Always later\" is false for a report approved earlier the same UTC day:\n  both dates come from `computeReportValidUntil`, so they are equal. The\n  guide and the db README now say \"never earlier\". Also \"within three\n  years of it\" now says \"of launch\".\n- Guide A3 counted the silent SUBMITTED withdrawal as a conflict. It now\n  says two 409s beyond the register check plus one silent replacement,\n  matching B6''s framing.","tree":{"sha":"4e920ccd8a4f7e69e730d369b2e742e8335ff872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/4e920ccd8a4f7e69e730d369b2e742e8335ff872"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e920ccd8a4f7e69e730d369b2e742e8335ff872\nparent 9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1790169115 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790169115 +0000\n\nfeat(doe): drop the salary renewal window (#1540)\n\n* feat(doe): drop the salary renewal window\n\nA company may now file a salary report whenever it likes. The rule that\nrefused a submission while the current report was due more than six months\nout is removed entirely — no toggle, no env flag — at the project owners''\nrequest (22 Sept 2026).\n\nThe remaining refusals are unchanged: a 404 when nothing covers the\ncompany''s equality obligation, and a 409 when a sibling salary report is\nIN_REVIEW or POSTPONED. Those duplicate guards are what stop runaway\nrefiling now that timing no longer does.\n\n**The eligibility endpoint reports what filing early costs.** The 3-year\nterm still runs from the approval date, so time left on the current\ncertificate is forfeited rather than carried over. `earliestNewDueAt` —\nthe deadline a report filed now would earn if approved today — sits\nbeside `dueAt`, and is returned whether or not the company is eligible.\n`RENEWAL_WINDOW_NOT_OPEN` and `earliestSubmissionDate` are gone; `reason`\nhas one member left, `MISSING_EQUALITY_REPORT`.\n\n**One definition of the 3-year term.** `computeReportValidUntil` is lifted\nout of `approve()` so the date the endpoint quotes cannot drift from the\none approval writes. It uses `setUTCFullYear` where the inline code used\nthe local variant, making `day-boundaries.ts` consistent with its own\nrule. Iceland is UTC, so behaviour is unchanged.\n\nThe gate was only ever enforced behind `API_ENV === ''prod''`, while the\neligibility route evaluated it everywhere — the two disagreed outside\nproduction all along. No migration: `next_salary_report_due_at` keeps\nevery other reader (overdue, reminders, register status, expiry filters).\n\n* fix(doe): address review on the renewal-window removal\n\n- One `REPORT_VALIDITY_YEARS`. `day-boundaries.ts` had declared a second\n  one beside the `constants.ts` copy that `remedy-date.ts` uses, so the\n  validity term and the remedy cap had two sources. It now imports the\n  existing constant, whose warning about the inline copy in `approve()` is\n  resolved.\n- `approve()` still said the next-due date is what the renewal-window\n  check reads. It now names the readers that remain.\n- The partner 409 lists (guide §B7, the status table, the submit route''s\n  description, `PartnerResponse`) left out the cross-type `providerId`\n  conflict, which is reachable here. The status table also contradicted\n  §B7 on island.is-filed POSTPONED siblings.\n- `submitSalary`''s comment said the early-filing cost is \"shown to the\n  applicant\". Nothing shows it yet; it is reported so the portal can.\n- \"It never does\" (guide §B2) and \"never true\" (db README) now say what\n  they rest on: approval-set deadlines, and the launch cohort''s seeded\n  dates, all inside three years.\n- The `day-boundaries.ts` header no longer cites the portal''s \"frá og með\"\n  display, which was `earliestSubmissionDate`.\n\n* docs(doe): finish the 409 lists and the deadline premise\n\nSecond review round.\n\n- The cross-type `providerId` 409 is symmetric: `createEquality` runs the\n  same check, so the equality route''s lists (guide A3, the route''s OpenAPI\n  description) now name it too, matching the salary side and the status\n  table.\n- Guide §B2 stated \"`dueAt` is three years from some past approval\" as a\n  general fact and hedged afterwards. For a deadline carried over from the\n  old register it is data, not a rule, so the approval case comes first\n  and the launch-data bound is stated as what it is.\n- `submitSalary`''s comment had a broken wrap and left out the tuple 409.\n\n* docs(doe): say \"never earlier\", and count the equality conflicts as B6 does\n\nThird review round, wording only.\n\n- \"Always later\" is false for a report approved earlier the same UTC day:\n  both dates come from `computeReportValidUntil`, so they are equal. The\n  guide and the db README now say \"never earlier\". Also \"within three\n  years of it\" now says \"of launch\".\n- Guide A3 counted the silent SUBMITTED withdrawal as a conflict. It now\n  says two 409s beyond the register check plus one silent replacement,\n  matching B6''s framing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9AbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX1MQAKapq/PXpcVgN9paFlvcw/yf\nMFBEc8E+WtVziKoNduk7D5ZW/6dl+sCbErD/F9tweAmHYxhMPK0jPNTtif+3GEOr\nGk3VSi7OhWiom29wBACxLU+z8084Zi2IYHAgwNwsAv5KV57A6vnSKSPLUyzhkQ+S\nvuZvqP7a0OrAIWU7xIPeaMKS6LSlO25kFNaSEsuHCO+H4+RawNczeTPeiMikTjnJ\nLUfuKm3kopc86JFMbSkpKrVUuxmjo5YghAneo04g3irFYVBIn5SxT1TwnosGBlWX\nZOV+3RIn5IR/OB3PFPzT6yzeB6eGdugUc+H298iXw+v7VGnY/kIPMxCed4PdMt/C\npjW4HlBwOK+CYh9PK+NN9q/0Bx4tXO6XaHjbT9Fli9t73B9OzRwupTxU5MrPFgAj\nw1u4NZrl1fQ8pQ1D1dc1fe9N9CpvuVi/f7dm5AxFWjtgk1vQhE983QMP62cAqMmt\nsnWP5jZ99ckE3mQENcj1FkvDoWNYK1jzLvSu5lLaVl4dnQZ5YFz9mZM/TWpNWuTi\nAwHNrUaSkfV3X1IZxrdtVvQ+SEd9gBxqheklXjAmW84Sz5kGnnlc5/LBfI38v0/o\nDW55jPkGDRCxabdTA6A3B0P0It5XFgTuQH6Z5+S/tiUQSMDI2p9c/sXSXfwGMQfM\n1BqqWLDs9deP0V/c7rj5\n=Bmzn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:11:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDA1NmY5M2I1NWNiMWFmMDU4MmNjZTJmYTE0Mjk1MWQ1NzlkMDU1Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814","sha":"9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814"}],"sha":"056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/056f93b55cb1af0582cce2fa142951d579d055cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:24:50Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:24:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doe): make the salary analysis an optional dry run (#1539)\n\n* feat(doe): make the salary analysis an optional dry run\n\nIt was the first half of a two-step submission and its own description said so:\n\"not optional in practice\". Phase 3 moved detection into the submit, so the\nround trip it existed for is gone and the route becomes what it should have\nbeen — a rehearsal. Send a payload, learn whether it validates and what it would\nproduce, commit nothing.\n\nIts own rate-limit bucket, and the reason is the vendor rather than us. A dry run\ndoes strictly less work than the submission it rehearses, so cost is not the\nargument; the argument is that rehearsing as often as an extract changes would\notherwise spend the same per-key allowance the *filing* needs, and an afternoon\nof debugging could leave a company unable to submit its report. The route also\nskips the surface-wide bucket, because counting against both would leave that\nfailure exactly where it was.\n\nApiKeyThrottlerGuard grows an abstract base so the two buckets are two guards\nwith one tracker rather than one guard with a branch. Nothing about the existing\nper-key behaviour changes.\n\nLocked exactly as before: full guard chain, the salary:submit scope it already\ncarried, @RequireActiveCompany from the controller. Nothing here is less\nsensitive than a submission — it simply does not store the result — so it gets\nno new scope and no public access.\n\nThe part worth reviewing is the spec. The route''s whole value is that it answers\nwith the submission''s rules, and \"both call assertParsedPayloadValid\" is an\nimplementation detail a refactor can quietly undo. So the test runs real\npayloads through both paths and compares verdicts. Mutation-checked: pointing\nthe preview at the weaker assertParsedPayloadIntegrity fails it on the\nweight-total case, which is the cross-field rule only the stronger one enforces\n— exactly the drift this codebase has been caught by three times.\n\nGuide: B4 is now marked optional and says what it is for, B5 no longer tells you\nto partition \"the ordinals from B4\", and the warning that an edit between B4 and\nB6 could reshuffle the detected set is gone, because the payload now crosses\nonce. Also removes two things phase 3 left behind: the outliersPostponed row in\nthe B6 body table, and the deferral paragraph telling vendors a postponed report\ncan only be finished on island.is.\n\n* docs(doe): record phase 4, and what it found already done\n\nMost of phase 4 was already true: the input shape, payDispersion''s placement,\nand the shared validator. What was missing was the throttle, the framing, and a\ntest holding the shared validation in place rather than a comment claiming it.\n\nAlso records that the throttle''s stated rationale was wrong. \"Optional and\nrepeatable\" reads as a cost defence, and a dry run costs less than the\nsubmission it rehearses; the real reason is that rehearsing must not spend the\nallowance filing needs.\n\nThat closes every phase in this plan except the calibration run, which needs\nreal documents rather than code.\n\n* fix(doe): finish the dry run''s throttle separation\n\nThree things the review of this branch turned up, all in work from the previous\ncommit.\n\nThe published rate-limit contract had stopped matching the code. Skipping the\nsurface-wide bucket on the dry run made two statements in the guide false: the\nper-key allowance is no longer \"across the whole surface\", and the X-RateLimit-*\nheaders a vendor is told to read do not appear on that route — the unsuffixed\nset belongs to the throttler named `default`, which that route now skips, and\nthe new bucket''s headers carry its name as a suffix. B4 had been updated to\nmention the separate allowance; the section that actually publishes the contract\nhad not. It now describes all three buckets, names the suffixed headers, and\nsays plainly that a client reading X-RateLimit-Remaining generically has to\nhandle its absence there rather than reading it as unlimited.\n\nThe separation itself was untested, which mattered more than it looks: it is not\none mechanism but two decorators agreeing. Without @SkipThrottle the dry run\nspends both budgets; without @UseGuards it is bounded by nothing but the per-IP\nceiling. Either way the route still works and still rate-limits, so nothing\nfailed. There is now a spec for it, built on a real Reflector against the actual\nhandler rather than a mocked one — mutation-checked by removing each decorator\nin turn, and each removal fails a different test.\n\nThat spec initially had the same blind spot as the code: every case constructed\nthe guard itself, so dropping @UseGuards would have left all of them green. The\nassertion that the route actually declares the guard closes it, using Nest''s own\nGUARDS_METADATA key rather than the string.\n\nAnd the 500/hour figure now says what it is: a starting point with no traffic to\nderive it from, with the reasoning for its order of magnitude and a note to\nrevisit it rather than treat it as settled.\n\n* fix(doe): address #1539 review should-fix items\n\n- Per-key throttler guards throw at boot when their bucket is not\n  configured, instead of failing open. The dry run skips the\n  surface-wide bucket, so an empty filter left it unlimited per key.\n- The dry-run guard also sends the standard Retry-After on a 429;\n  @nestjs/throttler only sends the suffixed one for non-default buckets.\n- Parity spec pins an expected verdict per row and adds the two\n  missing semantics-only rules (absent mandatory type, unclassified\n  employee), so a weakened shared validator no longer passes.\n- Guide: /partner prefix on the dry-run route, name all three suffixed\n  headers, document Retry-After.\n\n* fix(doe): address #1539 second review should-fix items\n\n- Parity spec grades only BadRequestException as a verdict on both\n  sides and rethrows anything else, so a crash fails the row instead\n  of passing as refused (or, on the submission, as accepted).\n- Guide: the standard Retry-After is promised for the per-key 429\n  only; the per-IP 429 carries no headers.","tree":{"sha":"70c8d462abaeb1f3752e5dd397894ad9c10a8755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/70c8d462abaeb1f3752e5dd397894ad9c10a8755"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814","verification":{"payload":"tree 70c8d462abaeb1f3752e5dd397894ad9c10a8755\nparent a9527ec32770fa147c3f064165b8f720877694d3\nauthor Jón Bjarni Ólafsson <dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com> 1790159090 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790159090 +0000\n\nfeat(doe): make the salary analysis an optional dry run (#1539)\n\n* feat(doe): make the salary analysis an optional dry run\n\nIt was the first half of a two-step submission and its own description said so:\n\"not optional in practice\". Phase 3 moved detection into the submit, so the\nround trip it existed for is gone and the route becomes what it should have\nbeen — a rehearsal. Send a payload, learn whether it validates and what it would\nproduce, commit nothing.\n\nIts own rate-limit bucket, and the reason is the vendor rather than us. A dry run\ndoes strictly less work than the submission it rehearses, so cost is not the\nargument; the argument is that rehearsing as often as an extract changes would\notherwise spend the same per-key allowance the *filing* needs, and an afternoon\nof debugging could leave a company unable to submit its report. The route also\nskips the surface-wide bucket, because counting against both would leave that\nfailure exactly where it was.\n\nApiKeyThrottlerGuard grows an abstract base so the two buckets are two guards\nwith one tracker rather than one guard with a branch. Nothing about the existing\nper-key behaviour changes.\n\nLocked exactly as before: full guard chain, the salary:submit scope it already\ncarried, @RequireActiveCompany from the controller. Nothing here is less\nsensitive than a submission — it simply does not store the result — so it gets\nno new scope and no public access.\n\nThe part worth reviewing is the spec. The route''s whole value is that it answers\nwith the submission''s rules, and \"both call assertParsedPayloadValid\" is an\nimplementation detail a refactor can quietly undo. So the test runs real\npayloads through both paths and compares verdicts. Mutation-checked: pointing\nthe preview at the weaker assertParsedPayloadIntegrity fails it on the\nweight-total case, which is the cross-field rule only the stronger one enforces\n— exactly the drift this codebase has been caught by three times.\n\nGuide: B4 is now marked optional and says what it is for, B5 no longer tells you\nto partition \"the ordinals from B4\", and the warning that an edit between B4 and\nB6 could reshuffle the detected set is gone, because the payload now crosses\nonce. Also removes two things phase 3 left behind: the outliersPostponed row in\nthe B6 body table, and the deferral paragraph telling vendors a postponed report\ncan only be finished on island.is.\n\n* docs(doe): record phase 4, and what it found already done\n\nMost of phase 4 was already true: the input shape, payDispersion''s placement,\nand the shared validator. What was missing was the throttle, the framing, and a\ntest holding the shared validation in place rather than a comment claiming it.\n\nAlso records that the throttle''s stated rationale was wrong. \"Optional and\nrepeatable\" reads as a cost defence, and a dry run costs less than the\nsubmission it rehearses; the real reason is that rehearsing must not spend the\nallowance filing needs.\n\nThat closes every phase in this plan except the calibration run, which needs\nreal documents rather than code.\n\n* fix(doe): finish the dry run''s throttle separation\n\nThree things the review of this branch turned up, all in work from the previous\ncommit.\n\nThe published rate-limit contract had stopped matching the code. Skipping the\nsurface-wide bucket on the dry run made two statements in the guide false: the\nper-key allowance is no longer \"across the whole surface\", and the X-RateLimit-*\nheaders a vendor is told to read do not appear on that route — the unsuffixed\nset belongs to the throttler named `default`, which that route now skips, and\nthe new bucket''s headers carry its name as a suffix. B4 had been updated to\nmention the separate allowance; the section that actually publishes the contract\nhad not. It now describes all three buckets, names the suffixed headers, and\nsays plainly that a client reading X-RateLimit-Remaining generically has to\nhandle its absence there rather than reading it as unlimited.\n\nThe separation itself was untested, which mattered more than it looks: it is not\none mechanism but two decorators agreeing. Without @SkipThrottle the dry run\nspends both budgets; without @UseGuards it is bounded by nothing but the per-IP\nceiling. Either way the route still works and still rate-limits, so nothing\nfailed. There is now a spec for it, built on a real Reflector against the actual\nhandler rather than a mocked one — mutation-checked by removing each decorator\nin turn, and each removal fails a different test.\n\nThat spec initially had the same blind spot as the code: every case constructed\nthe guard itself, so dropping @UseGuards would have left all of them green. The\nassertion that the route actually declares the guard closes it, using Nest''s own\nGUARDS_METADATA key rather than the string.\n\nAnd the 500/hour figure now says what it is: a starting point with no traffic to\nderive it from, with the reasoning for its order of magnitude and a note to\nrevisit it rather than treat it as settled.\n\n* fix(doe): address #1539 review should-fix items\n\n- Per-key throttler guards throw at boot when their bucket is not\n  configured, instead of failing open. The dry run skips the\n  surface-wide bucket, so an empty filter left it unlimited per key.\n- The dry-run guard also sends the standard Retry-After on a 429;\n  @nestjs/throttler only sends the suffixed one for non-default buckets.\n- Parity spec pins an expected verdict per row and adds the two\n  missing semantics-only rules (absent mandatory type, unclassified\n  employee), so a weakened shared validator no longer passes.\n- Guide: /partner prefix on the dry-run route, name all three suffixed\n  headers, document Retry-After.\n\n* fix(doe): address #1539 second review should-fix items\n\n- Parity spec grades only BadRequestException as a verdict on both\n  sides and rethrows anything else, so a crash fails the row instead\n  of passing as refused (or, on the submission, as accepted).\n- Guide: the standard Retry-After is promised for the per-key 429\n  only; the per-IP 429 carries no headers.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs6jyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwP8QABCZExAdn9mEDGz1RetH1Ofp\n340b815zzxWBgv67CMbzi2kdgsCUmiEI72u2D4s5vlUlgJ5p7SzbqvFmt6gbCHVL\nr/elw+BKyk5z0Z6QwUrU879HUIWNJNj/ZzWnKstu1F27+zeKzeWs3Uq6adSSw1MP\nzJFYkadxX0vfzGbzHGgc7+CkBWTAj0lcf7ZU5XxOe/ONyB/gVDYV54njMoxI0/fH\nvaZ7r+FwCO1bz1YVeFQpVHjlIC14Pj6wWsb2U9n5DQ26aO3MV7F5GG5f/uK25LVa\n1gr72vtqnl0JPMvdytuc767o0qowW5n0lObTUzSA7QzN0wfqaQwblZ0ML5ZXXIwA\nZjbxzfYujqfV+rN2zMGp0uwsYnOJBGLggf83nVHd4T/UZ/QE1Cl9uRx9GVmei4lQ\nuJchGoXWEweHMEodk6zl5UlDVsPeJxMXaj5t3/is1RVK30/+urvZCdx8pYpCuxCp\ncfzpssw8TA89tQ+8/lHLCy+EYc3FkRalKGk1rYo5vC29Y9eJIoJ4v+Mfk0Yneb9R\ngDnXSP6U2A/nmOlCqe7qhQg9ojo4Pyf/tGoKufNCOJJ3UvCntGaPalNxdlapgU5o\n4DxUjXo1pC6w5Kc46PawkHWXz0WTEsT526uN2wGUXtTaPe1ljGDItBmaoEUZfSQ8\n3vb+GSZ6uDUoau4OooOv\n=f89/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T10:24:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDljNjYzMDI1ODViY2I2MzdlZWFjOTI2NTBkNjdjZjI4YTNiMjU4MTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/a9527ec32770fa147c3f064165b8f720877694d3","sha":"a9527ec32770fa147c3f064165b8f720877694d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/a9527ec32770fa147c3f064165b8f720877694d3"}],"sha":"9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/9c66302585bcb637eeac92650d67cf28a3b25814"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/a9527ec32770fa147c3f064165b8f720877694d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:01:22Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:01:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doe): detect outliers at submit instead of before it (#1538)\n\n* feat(doe): detect outliers at submit instead of before it\n\nThe partner channel made a vendor run the analysis, model the outlier groups,\nand then submit the whole payroll again. That is wrong in two ways. The payload\ncrosses the wire twice, and any edit between the two calls reshuffles the set\nthe second call is validated against. Outliers are now detected during the\nsubmission itself, so what is scored is what was sent.\n\nThe part that made the old shape necessary was `outliersPostponed`: it asked the\ncaller to declare something only detection could answer. Set it on a clean\npayroll and the filing was refused for postponing nothing; leave it off with an\noutlier present and it was refused for want of groups. Neither answer is\navailable before submitting, so the flag forced the preview step it appeared to\nbe independent of.\n\nIt comes off the partner contract. Omitting the groups when outliers exist IS\nthe postpone, so nothing is lost by saying so: send groups and the report is\nSUBMITTED in one call, send none and it lands POSTPONED with the ordinals still\nowed in the response. A clean payroll is never refused either way.\n\nThe decision moves to where detection already happens. `postponeUnexplainedOutliers`\non CreateReportDto asks the question the other way round, and\nassertOutlierGroupsMatchDetected becomes resolveOutlierPostponement — one\nfunction, because \"is this postponed\" and \"do these groups cover the set\" are\nthe same question. island.is keeps `outliersPostponed` unchanged: it previews,\nso it genuinely knows.\n\nTwo things follow.\n\nPUT /partner/reports/:providerId/outliers, the exit from POSTPONED. Without it\nthis channel would publish a state nothing could leave, which is worse than the\nrefusal it replaces — the report exists, no reviewer can touch it, and the\nemployer would have to finish on island.is a filing their payroll system made.\nIt delegates to the same editOutliers the island.is route calls, with no\nwrapper: ownership, the all-or-none partition, the transition and the audit\nevents are all its business, so the channels cannot drift.\n\nAnd a POSTPONED sibling no longer blocks a re-file here. Since POSTPONED is now\nwhat a submission with outliers becomes rather than something a filer chose, the\n409 became a trap: a vendor that spots a payroll error after filing would have\nhad to explain figures it knew were wrong just to reach a state it was allowed\nto replace. withdrawPostponedSibling is opt-in, so island.is keeps the 409,\nwhere POSTPONED really is a deliberate \"explain later\". IN_REVIEW still\nconflicts on both — a reviewer is mid-workflow there, which is a different act\nfrom replacing something nobody has picked up.\n\nCreateReportResponseDto gains `status` and `unexplainedOutlierOrdinals`, taken\nfrom the set detection just produced rather than re-read, so the answer cannot\ndisagree with the groups written alongside it. The type checker found the three\nother places that build that response.\n\nNo migration. POSTPONED already means \"filed with unexplained outliers, a\nreviewer cannot pick it up\", which is exactly this state.\n\n* docs(doe): record phase 3, and the decision it reversed\n\nThe plan had kept the 409 on a POSTPONED sibling and written down its cost. That\ncost was acceptable while POSTPONED was rare; phase 3 makes it the ordinary\nlanding state, so the wart became the normal path and the decision is reversed —\non this channel only, by an opt-in flag rather than a change to the shared rule.\n\nAlso revises the security note that said the partner PUT must refuse anything\nbut POSTPONED. The sibling route already accepts IN_REVIEW, and refusing it here\nwould re-create a smaller version of the dead end this phase removes.\n\n* fix(doe): take the channel options off the wire contract\n\nThe design said \"neither of these is a field on either wire contract, and that\nis the point\". It was true of the partner DTO — omitted, whitelisted, rebuilt\nfrom a literal, and pinned by a spec — and false of the shared CreateReportDto,\nwhich is the @Body() of POST /api/v1/reports/salary. Both options carried\n@ApiOptionalBoolean there, so IsOptional + IsBoolean survived whitelisting and\nany authenticated applicant could send withdrawPostponedSibling: true to retire\ntheir own deliberate postponement, or postponeUnexplainedOutliers: true to file\nPOSTPONED where the service means to answer 400.\n\nSame company throughout, so never a cross-tenant hole. What makes it blocking is\nthat the claim was false on the one surface nothing checked, and the partner\nspec asserting the opposite is what would have stopped anyone looking.\n\nThey are a separate argument now — CreateSalaryOptions, mirroring\nSubmitSalaryOptions one layer up — so the claim holds by construction. The new\nspec asserts it on class-validator metadata rather than on a rejected request,\nbecause doe-api runs whitelist without forbidNonWhitelisted: an unknown field is\nstripped silently, so there is no 400 to catch, and what made these settable was\nthe decorator registering validation for them. Mutation-checked by re-adding a\ndecorated field.\n\nThree more from the same review:\n\nThe sibling withdrawal was keyed on who is filing rather than on what is being\nreplaced, so a payroll vendor''s submission would retire a POSTPONED report the\nemployer had deliberately deferred on island.is — with no signal to either\nparty, since the vendor cannot see that report and the employer''s 409 naming it\nwould be gone. It now matches providerType, and the docblock that claimed\nisland.is was untouched says which half of that it meant.\n\neditOutliers wrote status: SUBMITTED with no status predicate. That was\nunreachable until this phase let a POSTPONED sibling be withdrawn; now a\nsubmission carrying withdrawPostponedSibling can retire the report while its\nexplanations are being written, and an unconditional write would resurrect a\nWITHDRAWN row as SUBMITTED — two in-flight salary reports for one company, the\ninvariant the company lock exists to hold. It is a compare-and-set, and zero\nrows affected is a 409.\n\nThe guide contradicted itself in five places and stated one thing that was never\ntrue. B5 still told vendors to send outliersPostponed: true (now a 400) and said\nthe partner API had no route out of POSTPONED (this PR adds one); the B6 body\ntable still listed the removed field; the sibling policy still said POSTPONED\ngives 409. And the new B7 text claimed outliersPostponed \"stays true after B9\" —\nit is derived from status === POSTPONED, so it flips to false exactly when B9\nsucceeds, which would have had a vendor conclude its PUT had not applied.\n\nAlso: the replay specs mocked a row with no status, so status: existing.status\npassed through untested while toEqual ignored it; the partner contract spec\nrestated the validation options as literals instead of importing the app''s, and\nmoves to the app so it can; and the new route had nothing pinning its scope.\n\nNot fixed, and it needs a running API: clientConfig.json still declares the old\nCreateReportResponseDto. It is curled from doe-api rather than generated from\nsource, so it cannot be written by hand without fabricating generator output.\nRecorded in the plan''s checklist, including that the generated-files CI gate\ndoes not cover that file.","tree":{"sha":"9c19019e69678029bfdcf6303f30e5003d60b2b8","ur