rl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/d336bbaaa852d00988a98bbcb0febb6f83364cdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T13:54:32Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T13:54:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(lg): await the category-type prefetch so the page hydrates (#1529)\n\n* fix(lg): await the category-type prefetch so the page hydrates\n\n`/flokkar-og-tegundir` threw \"Hydration failed because the server rendered\nHTML didn''t match the client\" on every hard load, and React discarded the\nwhole tree and re-rendered it client-side.\n\nThe page and its container were on two different data-loading contracts.\n`page.tsx` used the streaming pattern - an unawaited `prefetch()`, which\n`makeQueryClient` supports by dehydrating pending queries - while\n`CategoryTypeContainer` reads the overview through `useQuery` and renders a\nskeleton off `isPending`. So the server rendered the skeleton branch and the\nclient hydrated the resolved one. The repo''s own `nextjs-page` skill pairs an\nunawaited prefetch with `useSuspenseQuery`; this container deviates.\n\nAwaiting the prefetch is the smaller of the two consistent fixes. Converting\nthe container to `useSuspenseQuery` would suspend the entire route - the app\nhas no `<Suspense>` boundaries and this segment has neither `loading.tsx` nor\n`error.tsx` - costing the in-place skeleton and the inline `TRPCErrorAlert`.\n\n`prefetch` now returns its promise so callers can await it. `prefetchQuery` is\n`.then(noop).catch(noop)`, so awaiting it cannot fail the render; an API error\nstill reaches the client, which refetches and shows the alert. `retry: false`\nkeeps a dead API from holding the page through three backed-off retries.\n\nThe change-log prefetch is dropped rather than fixed. It was keyed `{}` while\nthe container queries `{ limit: 25 }`, so its result was never read - a wasted\nround-trip on every load. Server-rendering it instead would arm a new\nmismatch: `ChangeLogTable` formats timestamps with `date-fns/format`, which\nresolves in the runtime''s local timezone, so server and browser would disagree\nanywhere off GMT.\n\n* fix(lg): give the awaited route a loading fallback\n\nAwaiting the prefetch blocks the route render, and this app has no loading.tsx\nat any level, so a client-side navigation into /flokkar-og-tegundir held on the\nprevious page until the API answered - where it previously painted the\ncontainer''s own skeleton immediately. The route fallback restores that instant\nfeedback without touching the fix or the inline TRPCErrorAlert.\n\nAlso notes in the prefetch JSDoc that an awaited call needs a loading.tsx, and\nthat retry: false bounds the number of attempts rather than the wall-clock\nwait - a slow-but-alive API still stalls the render.","tree":{"sha":"f77ca423f352500d2b86e59300984fa6edb9599e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/f77ca423f352500d2b86e59300984fa6edb9599e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/d336bbaaa852d00988a98bbcb0febb6f83364cdd","verification":{"payload":"tree f77ca423f352500d2b86e59300984fa6edb9599e\nparent 85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789998872 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789998872 +0000\n\nfix(lg): await the category-type prefetch so the page hydrates (#1529)\n\n* fix(lg): await the category-type prefetch so the page hydrates\n\n`/flokkar-og-tegundir` threw \"Hydration failed because the server rendered\nHTML didn''t match the client\" on every hard load, and React discarded the\nwhole tree and re-rendered it client-side.\n\nThe page and its container were on two different data-loading contracts.\n`page.tsx` used the streaming pattern - an unawaited `prefetch()`, which\n`makeQueryClient` supports by dehydrating pending queries - while\n`CategoryTypeContainer` reads the overview through `useQuery` and renders a\nskeleton off `isPending`. So the server rendered the skeleton branch and the\nclient hydrated the resolved one. The repo''s own `nextjs-page` skill pairs an\nunawaited prefetch with `useSuspenseQuery`; this container deviates.\n\nAwaiting the prefetch is the smaller of the two consistent fixes. Converting\nthe container to `useSuspenseQuery` would suspend the entire route - the app\nhas no `<Suspense>` boundaries and this segment has neither `loading.tsx` nor\n`error.tsx` - costing the in-place skeleton and the inline `TRPCErrorAlert`.\n\n`prefetch` now returns its promise so callers can await it. `prefetchQuery` is\n`.then(noop).catch(noop)`, so awaiting it cannot fail the render; an API error\nstill reaches the client, which refetches and shows the alert. `retry: false`\nkeeps a dead API from holding the page through three backed-off retries.\n\nThe change-log prefetch is dropped rather than fixed. It was keyed `{}` while\nthe container queries `{ limit: 25 }`, so its result was never read - a wasted\nround-trip on every load. Server-rendering it instead would arm a new\nmismatch: `ChangeLogTable` formats timestamps with `date-fns/format`, which\nresolves in the runtime''s local timezone, so server and browser would disagree\nanywhere off GMT.\n\n* fix(lg): give the awaited route a loading fallback\n\nAwaiting the prefetch blocks the route render, and this app has no loading.tsx\nat any level, so a client-side navigation into /flokkar-og-tegundir held on the\nprevious page until the API answered - where it previously painted the\ncontainer''s own skeleton immediately. The route fallback restores that instant\nfeedback without touching the fix or the inline TRPCErrorAlert.\n\nAlso notes in the prefetch JSDoc that an awaited call needs a loading.tsx, and\nthat retry: false bounds the number of attempts rather than the wall-clock\nwait - a slow-but-alive API still stalls the render.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsTcYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9hcQADpvVe6vonUeEK4YpR3Y4zf7\nJ03EVHufoRK61CNHz8SPFz7tjVPdX0Cb3Abc/mJ2TC9TSazelDUzr/1YN/wmKHQj\nczJ3L+Mwgn3hePi5OhEvImRYqDxwokIxc9tCunqsTO7nEVaAOmU7fpPXkePfzK8d\nyUFuYKumfxw/sALKPM0uFbJ2A8hp84Eu2OJm1r4DaoGH6zGHVvSMOI4D115gHJ5M\n4MTRubwcQqZJfRd3bx8SE3b9HHSFo1OYX6D/APsvuZRxlOKgOS8Z1ECcVddbtfZN\nXO6oa/Xmrv6+kY6u38xd9oyOOblVWdaaqfbWVnMhF3Eqv9iK2a8yD9F++c1XvF9P\ne+q9ofhwmUm2JN62s74HTpWx9xV3slkRbFNcu0i3ucaaGaTTbfgrdDDYDaKpFsVh\n2aZXPtpQPYvTmC/8/7s2twXHLeMIl3wvcszoQv1hupT/n089Z6FEK5VCgbK2aAGl\n+/gi38hLdkpKji9xys5lsTg0y+3TSJB8UXPSj8t6T8FvD+NeuT1WMCV+IDkZ30tn\n//Ix3nAzxqJiYSMPJR3UtqlZmwgAJI53f2bL8bsdsOoGtiVNwrGUBan5FfbPSI4n\n0Y73eEBwJz5/hMqCohA8hJduiZfl7pwOwm/4lqg/7JpErj9EjbJatgphKNVdWGS0\nrBqQhwx3M4iBf/cOMAub\n=ijct\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T13:54:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/d336bbaaa852d00988a98bbcb0febb6f83364cdd","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGQzMzZiYmFhYTg1MmQwMDk4OGE5OGJiY2IwZmViYjZmODMzNjRjZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5","sha":"85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5"}],"sha":"d336bbaaa852d00988a98bbcb0febb6f83364cdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/d336bbaaa852d00988a98bbcb0febb6f83364cdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:41:56Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:41:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): stop modals crashing server-side rendering (#1420)\n\n* fix(shared): stop modals crashing server-side rendering\n\nModalBase and ParallelModal call createPortal(..., document.body) during\nrender. `''use client''` puts a component in the client bundle but it still\nserver-renders on the initial request, so any hard load of a page containing\none returns 500 with \"document is not defined\".\n\nModalBase gates the portal on `renderModal = !removeOnClose || open`, and no\ncall site passes removeOnClose, so it is true on the very first render. The\nmodal does not have to be open for this to fire - it only has to be mounted.\n`GET /flokkar-og-tegundir` in legal-gazette-web 500s on dev today; the page has\nbeen reachable since #1368 (2026-08-12). Client-side navigation never surfaced\nit because it does not server-render.\n\nBoth components now render the portal only after mount.\n\nThat alone would have swapped one bug for another: three effects in ModalBase\nread dialogRef.current on mount, and with the portal absent on first render the\nref is null, so initialVisibility and an isVisible that is already true would\nhave set state without ever calling dialog.showModal(). The root cause is that\nthe component drove the native <dialog> imperatively at call time while\nassuming the element already existed. showModal/closeModal now only move state,\nand a single effect keyed on [open, mounted] syncs the dialog element to it.\nThe cancel and click-outside listeners take `mounted` as a dependency for the\nsame reason.\n\nParallelModal also dropped its non-null assertion on #modal-root, which throws\nif the element is missing.\n\nVerified: renderToString on the ModalBase render path throws \"document is not\ndefined\" before the guard and renders clean after; tsc passes for shared-dmr-ui\nand all five web apps.\n\n* fix(shared): fall back to document.body when #modal-root is missing\n\n`if (!container) return null` turned a missing `#modal-root` from a loud\nthrow into an invisible no-op: the route would change and nothing would\nrender, with no console trace and no error boundary hit.\n\n`#modal-root` is declared in exactly one place — `ritstjorn/layout.tsx` —\nso any parallel-route modal mounted outside that subtree would silently\nshow nothing. Fall back to `document.body` instead. The backdrop is\nfixed-position, so the modal renders correctly wherever it is portalled,\nand a layout that forgot the mount point degrades to a working modal.\n\nThe pre-mount `null` is unchanged: that one is the SSR guard.\n\n* fix(shared): resolve the parallel modal''s portal target once\n\n`container` was recomputed on every render. If #modal-root were absent on\nthe first post-mount render and present on a later one, the portal target\nwould change identity: React remounts the subtree, `dialogRef` reattaches\nto a fresh <dialog>, and the effect that calls `showModal()` does not\nre-run because it was keyed on `mounted`, which has not changed. The\nmodal would end up mounted and invisible — the exact failure the\n`document.body` fallback was added to avoid.\n\nResolve the target once into state in the mount effect and key the\n`showModal` effect on `container`, so the target cannot change identity\nafter the first post-mount render, and the effect would re-run if it\never did. `container === null` before mount is still the SSR guard, so\n`mounted` is now redundant and goes away.\n\nNot reachable today — #modal-root is server-rendered in ritstjorn''s\nlayout and the only call site sits under it.","tree":{"sha":"15871def36ab07206777cbf45d365c6756e0e0ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/15871def36ab07206777cbf45d365c6756e0e0ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 15871def36ab07206777cbf45d365c6756e0e0ab\nparent ba665acae1aa37ebe5101e9b508c4b923d385c4b\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789990916 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789990916 +0000\n\nfix(shared): stop modals crashing server-side rendering (#1420)\n\n* fix(shared): stop modals crashing server-side rendering\n\nModalBase and ParallelModal call createPortal(..., document.body) during\nrender. `''use client''` puts a component in the client bundle but it still\nserver-renders on the initial request, so any hard load of a page containing\none returns 500 with \"document is not defined\".\n\nModalBase gates the portal on `renderModal = !removeOnClose || open`, and no\ncall site passes removeOnClose, so it is true on the very first render. The\nmodal does not have to be open for this to fire - it only has to be mounted.\n`GET /flokkar-og-tegundir` in legal-gazette-web 500s on dev today; the page has\nbeen reachable since #1368 (2026-08-12). Client-side navigation never surfaced\nit because it does not server-render.\n\nBoth components now render the portal only after mount.\n\nThat alone would have swapped one bug for another: three effects in ModalBase\nread dialogRef.current on mount, and with the portal absent on first render the\nref is null, so initialVisibility and an isVisible that is already true would\nhave set state without ever calling dialog.showModal(). The root cause is that\nthe component drove the native <dialog> imperatively at call time while\nassuming the element already existed. showModal/closeModal now only move state,\nand a single effect keyed on [open, mounted] syncs the dialog element to it.\nThe cancel and click-outside listeners take `mounted` as a dependency for the\nsame reason.\n\nParallelModal also dropped its non-null assertion on #modal-root, which throws\nif the element is missing.\n\nVerified: renderToString on the ModalBase render path throws \"document is not\ndefined\" before the guard and renders clean after; tsc passes for shared-dmr-ui\nand all five web apps.\n\n* fix(shared): fall back to document.body when #modal-root is missing\n\n`if (!container) return null` turned a missing `#modal-root` from a loud\nthrow into an invisible no-op: the route would change and nothing would\nrender, with no console trace and no error boundary hit.\n\n`#modal-root` is declared in exactly one place — `ritstjorn/layout.tsx` —\nso any parallel-route modal mounted outside that subtree would silently\nshow nothing. Fall back to `document.body` instead. The backdrop is\nfixed-position, so the modal renders correctly wherever it is portalled,\nand a layout that forgot the mount point degrades to a working modal.\n\nThe pre-mount `null` is unchanged: that one is the SSR guard.\n\n* fix(shared): resolve the parallel modal''s portal target once\n\n`container` was recomputed on every render. If #modal-root were absent on\nthe first post-mount render and present on a later one, the portal target\nwould change identity: React remounts the subtree, `dialogRef` reattaches\nto a fresh <dialog>, and the effect that calls `showModal()` does not\nre-run because it was keyed on `mounted`, which has not changed. The\nmodal would end up mounted and invisible — the exact failure the\n`document.body` fallback was added to avoid.\n\nResolve the target once into state in the mount effect and key the\n`showModal` effect on `container`, so the target cannot change identity\nafter the first post-mount render, and the effect would re-run if it\never did. `container === null` before mount is still the SSR guard, so\n`mounted` is now redundant and goes away.\n\nNot reachable today — #modal-root is server-rendered in ritstjorn''s\nlayout and the only call site sits under it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsRgECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkFcQAEbOwRXCXugsCi8KQ0GIjmnz\nVoFnWXLg75zP9WZywAou2CALKRYgzN4ymFnRlf9NjFLDi5k2XZqS5Q35/YHCvv7+\nCG+evxdZthWq7jOnfNpFyT/agHxwk+dzRBPnHbGBUWyJi72Zdok88bV7Fn2ub+Bl\nwrK7HpVXB5Gj/4HGnD4HA58AFWBDfMimallSj8rffJOxC9ylwa8UYdf8VWtrzJpx\nx8PT/UgOm2BArjcB1CWOAqVN7/nBSa4l/iXXCZ+8poS7k6OfdEiqXzh8cSC/z553\nT59LyPLcG49yR9npT0mg298SVqzf2sZoGoWy8CqHE9Ab11Ohk14vi47KVCQmWovd\n85Epx3izoC3QUEGGSXEz90lnHeKAG6WOp6CpftV1iLtXAHF0peHrwP5a/e+SNJ60\nSkv/mqH1KqdZqGh+pmCYuZreA5DNNhHyOzNO9R2sj4fafL+I0S2bDSdWiVyrwge7\nsd7ARDeNG8ATUYzeFI2l/4E9ntM83olp9kW9ZNa+6M45QplzsTzMbj6weA49J/Rw\ny+uFOnbSWqZ4ozi0JTHoBOpz7u3+fbt6q2EGOPgKyxOqtKZt+QUOSNNWeEaEKwab\nLHPjkbk0G1y/iQw9Gu1vuZeNlgYVHdbZArYNfjJwPg2RcDo6LW0QKqjnVhxmM0op\n5Wfb2meQ+9yhqEz6BXve\n=GxKC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T11:41:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDg1YjVkMDc0NzY2NjU5NWIzNDU5OTA3ZjNhOGFiNWE2ZDM2NTU2YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/ba665acae1aa37ebe5101e9b508c4b923d385c4b","sha":"ba665acae1aa37ebe5101e9b508c4b923d385c4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/ba665acae1aa37ebe5101e9b508c4b923d385c4b"}],"sha":"85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/85b5d0747666595b3459907f3a8ab5a6d36556b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24840451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/ba665acae1aa37ebe5101e9b508c4b923d385c4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:13:16Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T11:13:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ojoi): stop a slow fee-service call from stalling the case view (#1526)\n\n* fix(ojoi): Slow payment-status lookup delay ojoi\n\n* fix(ojoi): bound every x-road call and scope payment state to published cases\n\nReview follow-ups on the payment-status isolation.\n\n- Restrict the payment loading and error states to published or rejected\n  cases, so a draft keeps its informational line whatever the fee service\n  is doing.\n- Keep a cached payment status visible behind a staleness warning when a\n  refetch fails, and disable \"Senda til TBR\" while it is stale so a claim\n  cannot be created twice against an unconfirmed status.\n- Drop @Transactional() from postExternalPaymentByCaseId and give the claim\n  POST the same deadline as the status read, so the write path no longer\n  holds a database connection across the external call. The publishing flow\n  still passes its own transaction in.\n- Give xroadFetch a 30s backstop deadline so no x-road call can hang\n  indefinitely; callers needing a tighter bound still pass their own signal.\n- Stop logging xroadFetch arguments, which carried the Authorization header.\n- Extract the fee service deadline to a constant, and type the unbatched\n  procedure list against the router so a rename fails the build.","tree":{"sha":"8bcdf356d1fe51c66ca0270b0beeeb7fbf6f7820","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/8bcdf356d1fe51c66ca0270b0beeeb7fbf6f7820"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/ba665acae1aa37ebe5101e9b508c4b923d385c4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8bcdf356d1fe51c66ca0270b0beeeb7fbf6f7820\nparent f7eb802ff5b90dafcbce50eb71b8680ab26a3aa1\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1789989196 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789989196 +0000\n\nfix(ojoi): stop a slow fee-service call from stalling the case view (#1526)\n\n* fix(ojoi): Slow payment-status lookup delay ojoi\n\n* fix(ojoi): bound every x-road call and scope payment state to published cases\n\nReview follow-ups on the payment-status isolation.\n\n- Restrict the payment loading and error states to published or rejected\n  cases, so a draft keeps its informational line whatever the fee service\n  is doing.\n- Keep a cached payment status visible behind a staleness warning when a\n  refetch fails, and disable \"Senda til TBR\" while it is stale so a claim\n  cannot be created twice against an unconfirmed status.\n- Drop @Transactional() from postExternalPaymentByCaseId and give the claim\n  POST the same deadline as the status read, so the write path no longer\n  holds a database connection across the external call. The publishing flow\n  still passes its own transaction in.\n- Give xroadFetch a 30s backstop deadline so no x-road call can hang\n  indefinitely; callers needing a tighter bound still pass their own signal.\n- Stop logging xroadFetch arguments, which carried the Authorization header.\n- Extract the fee service deadline to a constant, and type the unbatched\n  procedure list against the router so a rename fails the build.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsRFMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA09YQACfzhYqg6KTlbdejY4+q1oCr\nr15OnO2FAa5a8Mfrf8HpCC42uThDOI0S6CNyTIosGJ5chyI8QNlP1Jh94Q3u8jrg\nGb40CAlXxOEylRR89srdAu639rne4mvIb5ZPW+h5O1nkkMPb4yOME5jMrIv7wyeS\n+JLb9rKcfk2H/HCGQSBDX633+0L5WuQAnfMR5mGac06631y5CMUKEHkeVOur5dsI\nxwnRUo0UeV3RX29uANytjy6N81coy9jUbrvSBuLcHm5MjFoozKefJNF1vLoXUstY\nB7a4mc8Ow/Csonbevr/rsj2w2Jb7exjsto+akK+94tECVJep1FRg1ymZxjaaRcWw\nbbqwkGeWTECEJJfgpE4eA4Jlpdfthd0ziOQcwk7wkmS46QlHKoDJ2G3elUFRZAK/\nvPuFtC1Ri5681OdA+AkA1QN4fHw1yNY9AxD09j4NSxiy5aEeyL0Rvbn/GFiMv9QD\nDNMVtOwcUi7KeMDyeQp8ABLxCtHraOS3q9MnN/jvq2iWUtCteeyKtYbLo9+Lvz5m\nB7/DNInHQCvZiHJsk4TIIpTlhBf85pyy5kgIZT+ame0AlyyMfgYc9Zcb9+GoBvL+\n4i/DRwRMmhgjQECr3cpyogssV7Lt70S28+uBmUtAAdTpP0MAqNyVWcbrQNyarqTg\n8XTJkmHyhOrgu/J6sYVs\n=ZJ8g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T11:13:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/user