os/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/f7eb802ff5b90dafcbce50eb71b8680ab26a3aa1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/0f6c2d8f95bd4b9758cc342801e642d1868c2d88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:33:58Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:33:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(doe): format four files the repo-wide prettier pass missed (#1527)\n\n`afea7d663` (#1525) formatted the repo with prettier 3.5.3 and turned the\n`formatting` CI job into a hard gate, but four files were left unformatted,\nso `yarn nx format:check --all` fails on `main` and every PR branched from\nit inherits the failure.\n\nReformat them with `yarn nx format:write --all`. The changes are pure line\nwrapping and markdown table column alignment — no tokens added or removed.\n`doe-modules` passes 1526 tests, and both `yarn nx format:check --all` and\n`yarn run -T prettier --check .` are now clean.","tree":{"sha":"38fe5f8a0665077943b49b50c85f28ad14d31321","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/38fe5f8a0665077943b49b50c85f28ad14d31321"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/0f6c2d8f95bd4b9758cc342801e642d1868c2d88","verification":{"payload":"tree 38fe5f8a0665077943b49b50c85f28ad14d31321\nparent afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789983238 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789983238 +0000\n\nchore(doe): format four files the repo-wide prettier pass missed (#1527)\n\n`afea7d663` (#1525) formatted the repo with prettier 3.5.3 and turned the\n`formatting` CI job into a hard gate, but four files were left unformatted,\nso `yarn nx format:check --all` fails on `main` and every PR branched from\nit inherits the failure.\n\nReformat them with `yarn nx format:write --all`. The changes are pure line\nwrapping and markdown table column alignment — no tokens added or removed.\n`doe-modules` passes 1526 tests, and both `yarn nx format:check --all` and\n`yarn run -T prettier --check .` are now clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsPoGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwDkQACS0I0hH96pPdwWBYCqWa8Fx\ngu64tcorBr3F4EuDsjjz1YA0n6nKo5WC72IzSe82uxNuo37mAil4FkNSyyK9LxW1\noZGRgbGMrQzeewImMV6Eze5yrhYs/3W/xarLwR5TlBAxUA9Zd+GjIFyMSmlB+QDD\nHATXKmP1VXtF7NyfegfkY3GxQ8brF+cuJqU61qhewuPurCVdEycXJ+exjRz4dMh4\nIJkXQENyXsTYFu0Mk5AFVeVSLqFtuu1arf3bG/bPZ5q1V1Bo15xn3aw5t7Vp2zxT\nDVE772YgDjlssizN/PKR6v5udiqFt/8ChlNhrLfgcWtG9B7qrxJRzfTEw48TPGES\nR0CR2YLbrTMyH5541McVZnVS9p/a8VvSv1vpE+kYC0klRkqyHhPl6LV4vFM0tpuk\nBtsPZyaSUv9UpvECPiwLBENmCkWVMzjxKL5XxjVJXEIAng4pmOSFedoPJWv9ZF3k\nQwvktGnpEHzmgXTA4osSlLSn+P4t1l/RQjxqOEud/y8ON7nbMn17hRbxVSVNswVd\ncu/Kg4A3pyujf0PlNRP3ygaz3yFTHGeLyAlQA9nBy/tAQDJ/SAP9vcN5CnUf6bqZ\nie9FwirCvghjCzcAu70VESmGrlRdMg90YxQYTbqaXEHBip4fa/poY+NdpCnvlVyS\nP9DjSULvY307n6AxEOXN\n=/v7Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T09:33:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/0f6c2d8f95bd4b9758cc342801e642d1868c2d88","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDBmNmMyZDhmOTViZDRiOTc1OGNjMzQyODAxZTY0MmQxODY4YzJkODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd","sha":"afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd"}],"sha":"0f6c2d8f95bd4b9758cc342801e642d1868c2d88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/0f6c2d8f95bd4b9758cc342801e642d1868c2d88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:16:28Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:16:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(shared): format the repo with prettier 3.5.3 and make the format gate fail (#1525)\n\n* chore(shared): format the whole repo with prettier 3.5.3\n\nThe formatting job in quality.yml runs `nx format:write --all`, which writes\nand then always exits 0, so unformatted code has been landing on main\nunchecked. 453 files were off prettier''s output.\n\nPure formatting. Verified mechanically:\n\n- `prettier --check .` is clean across the repo.\n- All 64 changed YAML/JSON files parse to identical structures before and\n  after (checked with js-yaml / jsonc-parser, canary-tested).\n- All 375 changed TS/TSX/JS files were AST-compared with @babel/parser; the\n  9 that differ are quoted-to-bare object keys and JSX text reflow, both\n  semantics-preserving.\n\nThe two generator-owned files the `generated-files` job re-derives\n(template-data.ts, sub-criterion-catalog.data.ts) were already prettier-3\nclean and are untouched, so that gate still passes.\n\n* ci(shared): make the formatting job actually check formatting\n\n`nx format:write --all` rewrote files inside the CI runner and then exited 0\nno matter what, so the job was decorative. `format:check --all` reports the\noffending files and fails, which is what the preceding reformat makes\npossible.\n\n* fix(regulations): keep the require() disables attached after reformatting\n\nTwo statements in the Fastify smoke test were 94 characters, so prettier\nwrapped `require(...)` onto its own line and the preceding\n`eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires` no longer\ncovered it — two lint errors plus two unused-directive warnings.\n\nAliasing the module type keeps each statement on one line, which is what the\ndirective needs. Verified: `nx lint regulations-api` is back to 0 errors, and\nthe smoke test still passes.","tree":{"sha":"8099619e6f8630820d17f3a3c32b299dd6fafd2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/8099619e6f8630820d17f3a3c32b299dd6fafd2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 8099619e6f8630820d17f3a3c32b299dd6fafd2e\nparent 154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789982188 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789982188 +0000\n\nchore(shared): format the repo with prettier 3.5.3 and make the format gate fail (#1525)\n\n* chore(shared): format the whole repo with prettier 3.5.3\n\nThe formatting job in quality.yml runs `nx format:write --all`, which writes\nand then always exits 0, so unformatted code has been landing on main\nunchecked. 453 files were off prettier''s output.\n\nPure formatting. Verified mechanically:\n\n- `prettier --check .` is clean across the repo.\n- All 64 changed YAML/JSON files parse to identical structures before and\n  after (checked with js-yaml / jsonc-parser, canary-tested).\n- All 375 changed TS/TSX/JS files were AST-compared with @babel/parser; the\n  9 that differ are quoted-to-bare object keys and JSX text reflow, both\n  semantics-preserving.\n\nThe two generator-owned files the `generated-files` job re-derives\n(template-data.ts, sub-criterion-catalog.data.ts) were already prettier-3\nclean and are untouched, so that gate still passes.\n\n* ci(shared): make the formatting job actually check formatting\n\n`nx format:write --all` rewrote files inside the CI runner and then exited 0\nno matter what, so the job was decorative. `format:check --all` reports the\noffending files and fails, which is what the preceding reformat makes\npossible.\n\n* fix(regulations): keep the require() disables attached after reformatting\n\nTwo statements in the Fastify smoke test were 94 characters, so prettier\nwrapped `require(...)` onto its own line and the preceding\n`eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires` no longer\ncovered it — two lint errors plus two unused-directive warnings.\n\nAliasing the module type keeps each statement on one line, which is what the\ndirective needs. Verified: `nx lint regulations-api` is back to 0 errors, and\nthe smoke test still passes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsPXsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsbsQAEeuID9vvqgSP+DHg08LYtcd\nZQ3B+F8EbxULPO1a0GESVhHkEYXRA42CKRGYmJdI+HzCTc0+v8vAnPUZ3tTS2ucz\n2lnQWIdy9L9b60rBfrnq+2M6IbXX1eME4P0naUrfz00NfPUxQ5y3lj4LJq9aQb9P\nnF3zn7YMce+9ZL4/VHqVimR0eae41lz+Nhna/+bHb0tzkd6ZmXZDD4hYwZlZU757\nmT/8RDgXPiUG3RJI7BjbdAQD+WXqZ5QHpS8HVeKNmvSNG2EwVJgrKfbhTIxrlIZx\nH3MCjTSytogyRzAfqtwiBjGGQ6edSAiBp962qHjJsehn5u39cvicYN959IV2n/CX\nYIV16xJ5jXseH0rPm3lmb7EBsWdt9x7iSzb107lIsB0lIgd0A2N+iV+OtInAuaNi\ntKJSbiT67DZpdcvGWBpVrJOZE5RxUZFYmg6EBrgVvtcSuiRP3vl65+L3FA3GKrTe\nrYKWtcmuiR7xjS75ApDmFxTzVTvmTp0wkEupiz6cnmRPD6javyBPJHuw3/pKlpW8\nSifmLSkJC6xfBpymHoaX2x9SLu2ojeJpB93X5R7Nh/jpTc1Z+PqdbwtoglB4VcMY\nnbgcWn7dzkrRCmLsi/uMm0SHKypufi0d0DeDFPgQLHAQz+4pcGWZmqDjFHlW/pko\n3lwUjkJAiFikBCbC5VJY\n=v8cm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T09:16:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGFmZWE3ZDY2M2ViMjdmNzA4ZTNjMGExYjVjNTcwYTIxZWJjNTcyYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da","sha":"154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da"}],"sha":"afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/afea7d663eb27f708e3c0a1b5c570a21ebc572bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92530555?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jonbjarnio","id":92530555,"login":"jonbjarnio","node_id":"U_kgDOBYPnew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonbjarnio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:46:42Z","email":"dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com","name":"Jón Bjarni Ólafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:46:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doe): seed a fileable company and close the scoring-model follow-ups (#1515)\n\n* feat(doe): seed a company a vendor can file for, and close the scoring follow-ups\n\nThe deferrals from both review rounds of #1508, and the seeder that was the\nreason the flow had never run end to end.\n\n**The seeder.** Filing on the partner surface needs an approved equality report\nstill in force and a complete scoring model to score against, and assembling the\nsecond by hand is about fifteen calls threaded through ids returned by the last.\nThat cost is why the submission path was only ever exercised as far as the\npreview, and why the defects those rounds found were found by reading. Company\nslot 31 now carries both halves: an APPROVED equality report valid three years,\nand the smallest model that reads VALID — one criterion of each mandatory type,\none sub-criterion each at 25, a three-þrep scale, one job assigned across all\nfour. Deliberately the floor rather than a showcase, so a tester who breaks it\nlearns what the validator says about their change rather than about seeded\ncomplexity. No PERSONAL criterion, which lets `personalSteps` be `[]` and a\nfirst run need no judgement data at all.\n\n**Parent locks on the two replace-whole writes.** Both destroy and re-insert, so\ntwo callers on the same scale or the same job interleaved and collided on the\nuniqueness the table holds — surfacing as a raw 500 rather than the last write\nwinning. Each now runs in one transaction with the parent row locked, following\n`ConfigService.updateByKey`. Validation stays outside the transaction in\n`setRoleStepAssignments`: it reads only the already-loaded tree, and refusing\nbefore opening one keeps the lock held for the write alone.\n\n**A cross-wired assignment is now unrepresentable rather than merely caught.**\n`scoring_role_step` carries `scoring_sub_criterion_id` denormalised from the\nstep''s own parent so the one-per-job-per-sub-criterion uniqueness can be a table\nconstraint, but nothing tied the two together: a row naming a þrep of\nsub-criterion A alongside sub-criterion B satisfied both single-column FKs, and\nthe expansion would emit B at A''s þrep order — a silently wrong score. The\nservice refuses it and so does the expander, but neither is the table''s\nguarantee. A composite FK onto `(id, scoring_sub_criterion_id)` replaces the\nsingle-column one; verified by attempting exactly that insert, which the\ndatabase now rejects.\n\nTwo indexes duplicated the leading column of a UNIQUE constraint declared three\nlines above them, so they were write cost on tables the replace-whole writes\nrewrite in bulk. Dropped. `scoring_sub_criterion_step_id` — an FK with ON DELETE\nCASCADE, exercised on every scale replace — had no index at all, and now does.\n\n**The reason list no longer truncates in silence.** `MAX_REASONS` capped it and\nsaid nothing, so a badly broken model returned exactly 200 reasons and a caller\nworking through them would fix every one and still be refused. The notice costs\none slot.\n\n`WEIGHT_EPSILON`, `sum` and `approximately` are gone rather than shared: the\nweight rule moved to the filing gate in the last round, which left all three\nunused here. And `scoring_role_step` joins the join-table exceptions in the db\nREADME, since it is the one scoring table with no `updated_at`.\n\n* fix(doe): let the scoring writes join the request transaction instead of escaping it\n\nThe `sequelize.transaction()` wrapper on the two replace-whole writes read like\nit added atomicity and removed it. With no parent in its options it does not\nnest under CLS, so it opened a top-level transaction on a second pooled\nconnection: the destroy and bulkCreate committed immediately and survived the\nrollback CLSMiddleware performs on any non-2xx, leaving the scale replaced — and\nevery assignment onto the old þrep cascade-deleted — behind a response that\nreported failure.\n\nMeasured on both sides, through the running partner API:\n\n  without the wrapper  PUT that fails after the writes → 400, scale unchanged\n  with the wrapper     the same request never returns at all\n\nThe hang is the same defect seen from the other end. The second connection waits\non the FOR UPDATE the ambient transaction holds, and because the ambient side is\nonly idle-in-transaction rather than waiting back, Postgres sees no cycle to\nbreak.\n\nSo both writes now run on the ambient request transaction, and the FOR UPDATE —\nwhich was the part genuinely missing — is unconditional rather than taken only\nwhen a caller passed a transaction. Twelve concurrent replaces of one scale all\nreturn 200 and leave a coherent 1..6, where interleaving would have collided on\nUNIQUE (scoring_sub_criterion_id, step_order).\n\nAlso in this pass:\n\n- `scoring_role_step.scoring_sub_criterion_id` gets an index. It is an\n  ON DELETE CASCADE column whose only covering index has it as the trailing\n  member, so `deleteSubCriterion` cascaded through an unusable prefix — the same\n  reasoning the migration already applied to its sibling column.\n- The composite FK''s ADD CONSTRAINT is preceded by a check that names how many\n  rows are cross-wired, rather than aborting with only a constraint name.\n- The truncation notice is no longer lost. The filing gate fills before the\n  validator''s own bag does and reports it in an issue scoped REPORT, which the\n  model-level scope filter drops — so a saturated list said nothing about being\n  cut short. The fact now crosses the filter even though the sentence does not,\n  and the notice is scoped MODEL, since the scope enum documents CRITERIA\n  exhaustively and truncation is none of those things.\n- The seeder is idempotent. Its ids were minted from a running counter, so\n  ON CONFLICT (id) could never fire; the equality-report block was unguarded\n  entirely and aborted the whole seeder on the second dev-init, before the\n  scoring model was reached. Three consecutive runs now leave one copy.\n- db/README.md documents the composite FK, the UNIQUE it references and both\n  indexes; the stale column comment is re-issued from the new migration, since\n  editing an applied one would change nothing in a database that has run it.\n- Specs pin the lock on both paths and the truncation notice. Verified by\n  mutation: dropping the lock from the role path alone now fails a test, which\n  it did not before.\n\n* fix(doe): make the seeder survive an API edit, and correct two comments that measurement contradicted\n\nThe seeder''s guards arbitrated on `id` where the constraint that can actually\ncollide is a UNIQUE over other columns. `setSteps` and `setRoleStepAssignments`\nreplace a scale and an assignment set with fresh uuids, so once a tester has done\nthe thing this seeder exists to let them do, the seeded rows are gone but rows at\nthe same `(scoring_sub_criterion_id, step_order)` and `(scoring_role_id,\nscoring_sub_criterion_id)` remain — and `ON CONFLICT (id)` slid straight past\nthem into a duplicate-key abort.\n\nFixing that surfaced a second layer the guards alone could not reach: once the\nþrep guard correctly declines to re-create the seeded rows, an assignment naming\n`stepIds[i][1]` points at a row that does not exist, and the seeder fails on the\ncomposite FK instead. So assignments now resolve their þrep by *order* against\nthe table rather than naming an id. Verified in all three states — fresh, re-run\nuntouched, and re-run after an edit — with the tester''s own þrep and their chosen\norder left in place rather than overwritten.\n\n`down()` now deletes by company and takes `doe_api_key` with it. Six of the nine\nFKs into `company` are NO ACTION, and the header tells a tester to issue a key,\nso the documented workflow was exactly what made `down()` fail — after it had\nalready deleted the equality report. A filed salary report still blocks it;\n`report` has eleven NO ACTION children and unpicking that from a seeder would be\na second copy of a cascade the schema should own, so the comment says so plainly\nrather than half-doing it.\n\nTwo comments asserted mechanisms that measurement contradicts, both corrected:\n\n- The seeder claimed the old ids were non-deterministic. They were not: `nextUid`\n  was a module-level `let` re-initialised per `sequelize-cli` process and\n  consumed in a fixed order. Ran the previous version twice in separate processes\n  and diffed the id lists — byte-identical. Fixed ids are still right, for a\n  different reason, and the comment now gives that one.\n- `setRoleStepAssignments` claimed the composite FK turns the cross-endpoint race\n  into a raw 500. Raced both flows against Postgres with and without\n  m-20260915 applied: identical either way, only the constraint''s name differs.\n  Two outcomes are reachable — 23503 when the scale is replaced first, 40P01 when\n  the two cross each other''s row locks — and the race predates this change\n  entirely. The comment now says which is which and that it is pre-existing.\n\nAlso:\n\n- `findOwnedRole` moved back ahead of the validation loop. Behind it, an unknown\n  job sent with an invalid body returned 400 instead of 404, so the status\n  depended on the payload. The only covering test passed `assignments: []`,\n  which skips the loop, so it held either way; pinned now in both directions and\n  checked by mutation.\n- `scoring_role_step.scoring_sub_criterion_id` index, the composite FK and the\n  UNIQUE behind it are now in DIAGRAM.md, which still drew the single-column FK\n  while README.md described the composite one.\n- The migration''s pre-flight names the offending `scoring_role_step.id` values\n  rather than only counting them.\n- The partner API gets the `middleware-mounting.spec.ts` both siblings already\n  have. It is the app whose atomicity depends on `CLSMiddleware` being reached,\n  and it had no test that it is. Checked what it actually catches: on Express\n  5.2.1 both `''*''` and `''{*splat}''` mount, so it pins \"matches nothing\", which\n  is the failure that would silently un-transaction every request.","tree":{"sha":"ff2d3ade83fb6d4336bff16570f9e0231e32269a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/ff2d3ade83fb6d4336bff16570f9e0231e32269a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da","verification":{"payload":"tree ff2d3ade83fb6d4336bff16570f9e0231e32269a\nparent 52fc34ca933c54f685e9dd21e92b3ca01acfb03b\nauthor Jón Bjarni Ólafsson <dev.jonbjarni@gmail.com> 1789980402 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789980402 +0000\n\nfeat(doe): seed a fileable company and close the scoring-model follow-ups (#1515)\n\n* feat(doe): seed a company a vendor can file for, and close the scoring follow-ups\n\nThe deferrals from both review rounds of #1508, and the seeder that was the\nreason the flow had never run end to end.\n\n**The seeder.** Filing on the partner surface needs an approved equality report\nstill in force and a complete scoring model to score against, and assembling the\nsecond by hand is about fifteen calls threaded through ids returned by the last.\nThat cost is why the submission path was only ever exercised as far as the\npreview, and why the defects those rounds found were found by reading. Company\nslot 31 now carries both halves: an APPROVED