ion_id, step_order).\n\nAlso in this pass:\n\n- `scoring_role_step.scoring_sub_criterion_id` gets an index. It is an\n  ON DELETE CASCADE column whose only covering index has it as the trailing\n  member, so `deleteSubCriterion` cascaded through an unusable prefix — the same\n  reasoning the migration already applied to its sibling column.\n- The composite FK''s ADD CONSTRAINT is preceded by a check that names how many\n  rows are cross-wired, rather than aborting with only a constraint name.\n- The truncation notice is no longer lost. The filing gate fills before the\n  validator''s own bag does and reports it in an issue scoped REPORT, which the\n  model-level scope filter drops — so a saturated list said nothing about being\n  cut short. The fact now crosses the filter even though the sentence does not,\n  and the notice is scoped MODEL, since the scope enum documents CRITERIA\n  exhaustively and truncation is none of those things.\n- The seeder is idempotent. Its ids were minted from a running counter, so\n  ON CONFLICT (id) could never fire; the equality-report block was unguarded\n  entirely and aborted the whole seeder on the second dev-init, before the\n  scoring model was reached. Three consecutive runs now leave one copy.\n- db/README.md documents the composite FK, the UNIQUE it references and both\n  indexes; the stale column comment is re-issued from the new migration, since\n  editing an applied one would change nothing in a database that has run it.\n- Specs pin the lock on both paths and the truncation notice. Verified by\n  mutation: dropping the lock from the role path alone now fails a test, which\n  it did not before.\n\n* fix(doe): make the seeder survive an API edit, and correct two comments that measurement contradicted\n\nThe seeder''s guards arbitrated on `id` where the constraint that can actually\ncollide is a UNIQUE over other columns. `setSteps` and `setRoleStepAssignments`\nreplace a scale and an assignment set with fresh uuids, so once a tester has done\nthe thing this seeder exists to let them do, the seeded rows are gone but rows at\nthe same `(scoring_sub_criterion_id, step_order)` and `(scoring_role_id,\nscoring_sub_criterion_id)` remain — and `ON CONFLICT (id)` slid straight past\nthem into a duplicate-key abort.\n\nFixing that surfaced a second layer the guards alone could not reach: once the\nþrep guard correctly declines to re-create the seeded rows, an assignment naming\n`stepIds[i][1]` points at a row that does not exist, and the seeder fails on the\ncomposite FK instead. So assignments now resolve their þrep by *order* against\nthe table rather than naming an id. Verified in all three states — fresh, re-run\nuntouched, and re-run after an edit — with the tester''s own þrep and their chosen\norder left in place rather than overwritten.\n\n`down()` now deletes by company and takes `doe_api_key` with it. Six of the nine\nFKs into `company` are NO ACTION, and the header tells a tester to issue a key,\nso the documented workflow was exactly what made `down()` fail — after it had\nalready deleted the equality report. A filed salary report still blocks it;\n`report` has eleven NO ACTION children and unpicking that from a seeder would be\na second copy of a cascade the schema should own, so the comment says so plainly\nrather than half-doing it.\n\nTwo comments asserted mechanisms that measurement contradicts, both corrected:\n\n- The seeder claimed the old ids were non-deterministic. They were not: `nextUid`\n  was a module-level `let` re-initialised per `sequelize-cli` process and\n  consumed in a fixed order. Ran the previous version twice in separate processes\n  and diffed the id lists — byte-identical. Fixed ids are still right, for a\n  different reason, and the comment now gives that one.\n- `setRoleStepAssignments` claimed the composite FK turns the cross-endpoint race\n  into a raw 500. Raced both flows against Postgres with and without\n  m-20260915 applied: identical either way, only the constraint''s name differs.\n  Two outcomes are reachable — 23503 when the scale is replaced first, 40P01 when\n  the two cross each other''s row locks — and the race predates this change\n  entirely. The comment now says which is which and that it is pre-existing.\n\nAlso:\n\n- `findOwnedRole` moved back ahead of the validation loop. Behind it, an unknown\n  job sent with an invalid body returned 400 instead of 404, so the status\n  depended on the payload. The only covering test passed `assignments: []`,\n  which skips the loop, so it held either way; pinned now in both directions and\n  checked by mutation.\n- `scoring_role_step.scoring_sub_criterion_id` index, the composite FK and the\n  UNIQUE behind it are now in DIAGRAM.md, which still drew the single-column FK\n  while README.md described the composite one.\n- The migration''s pre-flight names the offending `scoring_role_step.id` values\n  rather than only counting them.\n- The partner API gets the `middleware-mounting.spec.ts` both siblings already\n  have. It is the app whose atomicity depends on `CLSMiddleware` being reached,\n  and it had no test that it is. Checked what it actually catches: on Express\n  5.2.1 both `''*''` and `''{*splat}''` mount, so it pins \"matches nothing\", which\n  is the failure that would silently un-transaction every request.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsO7yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjrwQAFDGEW/1tbdIM0GREU5BvqDn\nKhhSufpHFi3g3cs6uGY+wTJvB1fkX06Nu90PtYAc3s5gsl2Fc9egF1/1PLF/UaGI\nWDwVmcIlSYDCphfj+/00vMMEM4eKjlidup1ncCrVgHZztS4UyBfwR4d4XRRHAStg\nKlK92u+8recn1pesT2vqmO1/H2QgUkI6CFI1M1i5KG6bZTzBQDlkzjchPxCQeayJ\n97IgMsn+/fvRwWoaILt3FDVZJWIkhxI1B6kUgxIUnUF8/WSFrqGanUk3etRk2CDp\nAkvnaR2Ekc9dkOLJkHA1yvkZk4X4J2gnoDKkeZAd8hv2ylAYwZjCJi6jVPsWaeNi\nkyrY/aqE4fWq3NAL6VE5Ygz7XMG56jiHCCiOBLvkFqpCMsT2NOTViajaJNgzjfRB\nKwAVPybnoD4gt4afENnXEcgU+FJ/jGZRkhKZ7vgMR+paBwECCYOzO4Eb/d5FZz+9\n2iUCSEcKgWiqs8TDJwQYrliocd0EsDOdosF0G/YS43FxsincSyS24vGf937tFKCp\na3C248Zht27m6R+7IIM3FsPjNNVcY8UqD9zSJW38Ha8i+pggfQb9Id5xIiL7a9sV\nmYKNmN9UzU17oTKB2TP8jySNqieupoDj/paywOeX03sv8mWYfoCLHThpA2fNygQN\nr3NvHgn9qWp+eXNsNFqQ\n=BrcK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T08:46:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDE1NDI5M2Y0YmQ3NzQwZmY5MTJlMzFkYjg1ODg4OGQyZjU1MzU3ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/52fc34ca933c54f685e9dd21e92b3ca01acfb03b","sha":"52fc34ca933c54f685e9dd21e92b3ca01acfb03b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/52fc34ca933c54f685e9dd21e92b3ca01acfb03b"}],"sha":"154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/154293f4bd7740ff912e31db858888d2f55357da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24840451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/52fc34ca933c54f685e9dd21e92b3ca01acfb03b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:06:00Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:06:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(doe): surface active company filters and fix report wording by type (#1521)\n\n* feat(doe): surface active company filters and fix report wording by type\n\nCompany register (Fyrirtæki)\n\n- Show every active filter as a removable tag above the table, with a\n  \"Hreinsa allt\" action. The panel only turned a collapsed accordion''s\n  heading blue, so a pre-filtered list read as the whole list.\n- Hide quarantined companies by default and move the control from\n  \"Staða > Annað\" to the \"Engin skilaskylda\" reveals, beside the\n  not-obliged and deregistered hides. Offering the same axis in both\n  places let two controls contradict each other. An explicit\n  `quarantined` request still lifts the hide, so filtering to companies\n  in var returns them rather than an empty page.\n- Add four \"aldrei skilað\" filters under \"Staða > Annað\": never filed an\n  equality plan or a salary report, each in an \"í kerfinu\" and a\n  \"né eldri gögn\" variant. Most companies were loaded from the retired\n  SharePoint register with no report row of their own, so the two\n  questions have very different answers and the list offers both. They\n  carry no obligation gate and do not lift the default hides.\n- Open a pre-filtered group in the submissions filter panel, so arriving\n  from a front-page card shows which filter is applied.\n\nReport timeline (Athugasemdir) and mail\n\n- An equality submission is a jafnréttisáætlun the company uploads, not a\n  skýrsla. The submitted, edited and auto-review timeline entries now pick\n  their noun from the report type; absent a type they read as before.\n- The external-comment mail called every report a \"jafnréttisskýrslu\" in\n  its subject and both renderings, which named the wrong thing for both\n  types. It now matches the deadline-reminder wording.\n\n* Fix after CR","tree":{"sha":"a696282969230e2f5e10e81593a042256143b67d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/a696282969230e2f5e10e81593a042256143b67d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/52fc34ca933c54f685e9dd21e92b3ca01acfb03b","verification":{"payload":"tree a696282969230e2f5e10e81593a042256143b67d\nparent 659d1eb381b6df916135564b7a1a36f9b014218b\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1789945560 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789945560 +0000\n\nfeat(doe): surface active company filters and fix report wording by type (#1521)\n\n* feat(doe): surface active company filters and fix report wording by type\n\nCompany register (Fyrirtæki)\n\n- Show every active filter as a removable tag above the table, with a\n  \"Hreinsa allt\" action. The panel only turned a collapsed accordion''s\n  heading blue, so a pre-filtered list read as the whole list.\n- Hide quarantined companies by default and move the control from\n  \"Staða > Annað\" to the \"Engin skilaskylda\" reveals, beside the\n  not-obliged and deregistered hides. Offering the same axis in both\n  places let two controls contradict each other. An explicit\n  `quarantined` request still lifts the hide, so filtering to companies\n  in var returns them rather than an empty page.\n- Add four \"aldrei skilað\" filters under \"Staða > Annað\": never filed an\n  equality plan or a salary report, each in an \"í kerfinu\" and a\n  \"né eldri gögn\" variant. Most companies were loaded from the retired\n  SharePoint register with no report row of their own, so the two\n  questions have very different answers and the list offers both. They\n  carry no obligation gate and do not lift the default hides.\n- Open a pre-filtered group in the submissions filter panel, so arriving\n  from a front-page card shows which filter is applied.\n\nReport timeline (Athugasemdir) and mail\n\n- An equality submission is a jafnréttisáætlun the company uploads, not a\n  skýrsla. The submitted, edited and auto-review timeline entries now pick\n  their noun from the report type; absent a type they read as before.\n- The external-comment mail called every report a \"jafnréttisskýrslu\" in\n  its subject and both renderings, which named the wrong thing for both\n  types. It now matches the deadline-reminder wording.\n\n* Fix after CR","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsGbYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeu8QADZ6HkdVe+lvlYOSSwYtD2ZA\n53V4VIYze0sTU+roFvTe/JNL0Ge3RlzvP45bk+0UOeSvHSrkil9QCLHaVrkeLpI4\nylWVl4GL3SDVayKA+Y4bj7/4KBFJuNRYeUncLgtYYoqWEuQVT6sdRCKzSJgAhKgd\naSboNaNb0329xjCFNMVWxMtfhSMiDcG81k+nVy0xlRzOX331Gvw/I8ZyB6Cz7dQd\nJNPS5rBc7SP3H/n18focItNv21PIlMTZa2qRyzOzStQD9jzIFeGzyaHV6k8T9JsI\nKGa5RT8/AQ76iozjMHEx4skclZk8SH5KIZeB88dB6nhhNCBTaJ+M1zyFk4MhREKi\ntKZkKW3PhH/0WjfGFE7vAAl75S/qoAqxKPyuaFSSzDxsKfAv6dxeCsjynoZBnUkW\nlAtSE0k/omxTB0p55r8OecL5IILqpLusEiUkdHh8RghWTBRQcUau/YNl35WJOLtm\nvA6ZgSvGjjXPVLFbrsycu4uZ5ftgePLUiG2JRPmKMrfIlxrZRA/kGQPd6iv93cv7\nvhxQXnq6AeuNuFTy+3x7fDQZV+hwncoBOsvXwC4YcEmzNe8QhxY62Zll6jeFlQFW\ngBt+nxoJ7VreVbAT/MuK