/api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/659d1eb381b6df916135564b7a1a36f9b014218b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:22:06Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:22:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): run the codegen prettier step through the root workspace''s bin (#1523)\n\n`node_modules/.bin/prettier` is prettier 2.2.0, not the 3.5.3 the root\npackage.json declares. `@dmr.is/regulations-tools` depends on the alias\n`cleanup-prettier: npm:prettier@2.2.0`; Yarn hoists it to\n`node_modules/cleanup-prettier`, its manifest still says `bin: prettier`,\nand the linker pointed the shared shim at that copy. `node_modules/prettier`\nitself is 3.5.3, so `nx format`, `yarn prettier` at the root, editors and\n`require(''prettier'')` all use 3 — only callers of the bare `prettier`\ncommand get 2.\n\n`nx:run-commands` puts `.bin` on PATH, so the six codegen targets that end\nin `prettier --write clientConfig.*` have been formatting with 2.2.0. They\nnow run `yarn run -T prettier`, which resolves the top-level workspace''s\nown dependency. Plain `yarn prettier` does not work here: five of the six\ntargets run inside a nested workspace with its own package.json, and Yarn\nanswers \"Couldn''t find a script named prettier\" there. `-T` is what makes\nit resolve from the root.\n\nThe shim itself is untouched; removing the collision means dropping the\nalias in regulations-tools, which is a separate repo.","tree":{"sha":"5861571f84fe3b0bb34c1063af9bffc6fa9d00f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/5861571f84fe3b0bb34c1063af9bffc6fa9d00f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/659d1eb381b6df916135564b7a1a36f9b014218b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5861571f84fe3b0bb34c1063af9bffc6fa9d00f6\nparent 7c05768c6313337fc9e4661f4267050474a24c34\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789744926 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789744926 +0000\n\nfix(shared): run the codegen prettier step through the root workspace''s bin (#1523)\n\n`node_modules/.bin/prettier` is prettier 2.2.0, not the 3.5.3 the root\npackage.json declares. `@dmr.is/regulations-tools` depends on the alias\n`cleanup-prettier: npm:prettier@2.2.0`; Yarn hoists it to\n`node_modules/cleanup-prettier`, its manifest still says `bin: prettier`,\nand the linker pointed the shared shim at that copy. `node_modules/prettier`\nitself is 3.5.3, so `nx format`, `yarn prettier` at the root, editors and\n`require(''prettier'')` all use 3 — only callers of the bare `prettier`\ncommand get 2.\n\n`nx:run-commands` puts `.bin` on PATH, so the six codegen targets that end\nin `prettier --write clientConfig.*` have been formatting with 2.2.0. They\nnow run `yarn run -T prettier`, which resolves the top-level workspace''s\nown dependency. Plain `yarn prettier` does not work here: five of the six\ntargets run inside a nested workspace with its own package.json, and Yarn\nanswers \"Couldn''t find a script named prettier\" there. `-T` is what makes\nit resolve from the root.\n\nThe shim itself is untouched; removing the collision means dropping the\nalias in regulations-tools, which is a separate repo.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrVceCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcAQQABM5LgoStfL3MIzGtuknHnMo\nBJFHTRl6JJvbKFBOgYQq+3+Ciqd1OXUr1KVgjshZBz0Kku5BFAIfJwGJ1SL4ViGL\nsiYdYGaYEfsxzssFL+W8VYC21ph9Cb32l380ZU2goTSrNXxdnpsICJMJ++TlJgtY\nAtsvbYO2YsfsRhhvI4C0IT5atLb07+Sajx/uebfuVB5pmjWdVarEnBt8MMa6dBdu\n84NQ75z6uTioEYPWm73r9Q8jT91b0TLQCrNOcD+ueNuVSY3z/2D5CGmDx/T3G/rm\n4CKEjT6pZiBCbe5BWZIZ3o/Zd1bOVAtFKdQsnvxHp01scpsR1hxQPFclv5Klst4b\nNSOrRYzWFJjNhk14/ci38NiudQjy1M9EwGZ3jmko/UQ+yM+vHkKU+zcolHiLWxuK\nfxEREQULyF+ItcDywlM7MHc282sNHrCxXIrU/Ga4B1fRT624oquX6th1AmVIJaK7\n0UV6hQdCk2JoxAAnVuO7XgyhbxmoL3OC2BZ5WI1AuuL3SzO+5iRh+A0gWnfsBBFT\n740axndK24zJlck6634LZ8yzDwBvlXgJAC4t/nkV2k3vtwFobB8z6Dw8yHK8mfet\nMZ7vrSLknCNT8vlT0zUJ8FXmUO76EQXMn7j6RH5kTyUb6GC6pfaSIpj+/RIhXkIq\nA+F0p5RikNiBGBoAcv2N\n=hT5U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T15:22:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/659d1eb381b6df916135564b7a1a36f9b014218b","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDY1OWQxZWIzODFiNmRmOTE2MTM1NTY0YjdhMWEzNmY5YjAxNDIxOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/7c05768c6313337fc9e4661f4267050474a24c34","sha":"7c05768c6313337fc9e4661f4267050474a24c34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/7c05768c6313337fc9e4661f4267050474a24c34"}],"sha":"659d1eb381b6df916135564b7a1a36f9b014218b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/659d1eb381b6df916135564b7a1a36f9b014218b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/7c05768c6313337fc9e4661f4267050474a24c34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T13:41:57Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T13:41:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(doe): scope the cited equality report to the submitting company (#1522)\n\n* fix(doe): scope the cited equality report to the submitting company\n\n`assertEqualityReportApproved` checked that the `equalityReportId` an\napplicant names on a salary submission is an APPROVED, in-force EQUALITY\nreport, and nothing else. It never asked whose. A company without a valid\nequality plan could file a salary report against any other company''s\napproved plan; the borrowed identifier, approvedAt and validUntil then read\nback on GET /application/reports/:providerId, and approval moved the\ncompany''s next_salary_report_due_at out three years. Reachable from the\npartner API as well as island.is.\n\nThe guard now takes the authenticated company and inner-joins\ncompany_report on it, so the report must cover the caller. Both callers\npass the submitter: the draft submit passes the company `findOwnedDraft`\nresolved, and the create path passes the parent company of the snapshot\nset. Not the caller''s payload in either case.\n\nThe join is on companyId alone, not `{ companyId, parentCompanyId: null }`.\nThat matches `findActiveEqualityForCompany`, which the eligibility and\nactive-report routes and `resolveEqualityCoverage` all answer from. Those\nroutes hand a subsidiary its group''s equality report id, so the submit\nguard has to accept that same id back; filtering to the parent row is the\nregression `resolveEqualityCoverage` already documents.\n\n404 with the same sentence as for an unknown id, so a caller cannot tell\n\"not yours\" from \"not there\".\n\nClaude Security F8.\n\n* fix(doe): restore the parent pin in withdrawInflightSibling\n\nThe previous commit dropped `parentCompanyId: null` from the in-flight\nsibling search alongside the intended change to\n`assertEqualityReportApproved`. The two queries answer different\nquestions: coverage flows down a group, so the equality-report join\nmatches a subsidiary on purpose; ownership of an in-flight filing does\nnot, so a subsidiary''s snapshot on its parent''s report must not resolve\nto the parent''s report. Without the pin a subsidiary''s own submission\nwithdrew a SUBMITTED parent report, or 409''d against an IN_REVIEW one\nand disclosed its providerId.\n\nAdds a test asserting the where shape, since none of the three existing\ntests constrained it. Rewords the new doc comments: the company id\nhanded to `assertEqualityReportApproved` from `ReportCreateService` is\nthe parent entry of a server-built snapshot set, not an authenticated\nprincipal, and the guard is only as strong as every caller keeping\n`companies[]` server-side.","tree":{"sha":"5a22cd3a9023e32a5538e158d6dde9edaf105ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/5a22cd3a9023e32a5538e158d6dde9edaf105ba9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/7c05768c6313337fc9e4661f4267050474a24c34","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a22cd3a9023e32a5538e158d6dde9edaf105ba9\nparent feb1507b61998c6a060c12cc805a83781ebc99c2\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789738917 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789738917 +0000\n\nfix(doe): scope the cited equality report to the submitting company (#1522)\n\n* fix(doe): scope the cited equality report to the submitting company\n\n`assertEqualityReportApproved` checked that the `equalityReportId` an\napplicant names on a salary submission is an APPROVED, in-force EQUALITY\nreport, and nothing else. It never asked whose. A company without a valid\nequality plan could file a salary report against any other company''s\napproved plan; the borrowed identifier, approvedAt and validUntil then read\nback on GET /application/reports/:providerId, and approval moved the\ncompany''s next_salary_report_due_at out three years. Reachable from the\npartner API as well as island.is.\n\nThe guard now takes the authenticated company and inner-joins\ncompany_report on it, so the report must cover the caller. Both callers\npass the submitter: the draft submit passes the company `findOwnedDraft`\nresolved, and the create path passes the parent company of the snapshot\nset. Not the caller''s payload in either case.\n\nThe join is on companyId alone, not `{ companyId, parentCompanyId: null }`.\nThat matches `findActiveEqualityForCompany`, which the eligibility and\nactive-report routes and `resolveEqualityCoverage` all answer from. Those\nroutes hand a subsidiary its group''s equality report id, so the submit\nguard has to accept that same id back; filtering to the parent row is the\nregression `resolveEqualityCoverage` already documents.\n\n404 with the same sentence as for an unknown id, so a caller cannot tell\n\"not yours\" from \"not there\".\n\nClaude Security F8.\n\n* fix(doe): restore the parent pin in withdrawInflightSibling\n\nThe previous commit dropped `parentCompanyId: null` from the in-flight\nsibling search alongside the intended change to\n`assertEqualityReportApproved`. The two queries answer different\nquestions: coverage flows down a group, so the equality-report join\nmatches a subsidiary on purpose; ownership of an in-flight filing does\nnot, so a subsidiary''s snapshot on its parent''s report must not resolve\nto the parent''s report. Without the pin a subsidiary''s own submission\nwithdrew a SUBMITTED parent report, or 409''d against an IN_REVIEW one\nand disclosed its providerId.\n\nAdds a test asserting the where shape, since none of the three existing\ntests constrained it. Rewords the new doc comments: the company id\nhanded to `assertEqualityReportApproved` from `ReportCreateService` is\nthe parent entry of a server-built snapshot set, not an authenticated\nprincipal, and the guard is only as strong as every caller keeping\n`companies[]` server-side.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrT+lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmRMQADXZ49g5abEOmPkYdknU/Kig\nUwlITFK5D7ceRhvQGiYeNmwZWQAuU8zhku9i0msAEANxp4e4SBW4AK1ofnOnK1L/\nj215U6aO6Zzy7x4NrNn0/ThVXnmWeY7B2jYYLGOUoOuyz4ntePlIpXPewKO7NdhY\nBpAVWjOAgptPbnTLT5f2PVYzsrlkxc9zLRMGue8yC854wGm20+LMaKiHT5fdfVD4\nOHp0WggHikAzCYbxEzblUZOuJN3vNsNnzzTUpBsh5DWtRfTdBxJI12xiPlvRxE1A\nKKIn+eVb8Eu00p5oIVZbYJW/TzDzxOohIkY4VAY5ls5DO+PMWbdRNhUH4jg4m0Mp\nJhf8Y84NLflNuph+4ovdENBysy54qdbgONKo93OBegG37bQQx3bKwOx6vDPO61n5\n6JvZ3VRLXmA0z6yklhmxzje9hMe+3KN7uSgxtnT/s9ZcakMiCoe++7uRLxJpIdr2\ngPv0tQCy6Z