UO8Z3403brbRPgn8WaYb9w08wxpoCislwpkznKpMM/RLCUQIL\nX1XFHD7n4tovFa4ITcws2FojPszmh2FA//vvM71JKX0ToiEBOT1ZFdu7ZOYbJOn4\niZiu9Ty9q5d4eXihKvF65Jm5sj966oyeLA0/DINJkFmc2n2VH0R1TibdgjDjatWC\ngzCOF/Jrm95UrRLIsv+ZjCqPWO4fsf4mnl4Nb9Zsv4npmdacfdqi+2HTGJLi9ANh\nnFi00kDjx1ww9DEPEcNYL4LbRiar3ulMw15EhpkqBNsR296df08RaRVyTIHGZU1R\nu14T0CIGEoTLIdbX9Yv+i5L5OGIlRflNlzC+ZbgcvMi/GwV9Nlwqqg40HYsZN1Wa\njUtDfDHA8GE0vrmwWjNqbMa3Zeo/ZhExRmD6D6wTvppcYyRUeRtmNty4vPilwIOA\nWNkN3sjtZ41tE2/+rYQsoYqSV2lkCRlwMPzRrPCAsnnQqYob3y7V9R+Rh/Yr/GNt\noQwWOuBb2gp+NDd0rNlxWTUBq8xnlZWnfiPSUq2EZBIvt+svk/fY7vmpY4ejmh2w\niQiGATZriOBjScp9AxRN\n=pvEl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T11:10:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/c36a740702a05d3d93764132f3a493fc74de1314","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGMzNmE3NDA3MDJhMDVkM2Q5Mzc2NDEzMmYzYTQ5M2ZjNzRkZTEzMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911","sha":"574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911"}],"sha":"c36a740702a05d3d93764132f3a493fc74de1314","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/c36a740702a05d3d93764132f3a493fc74de1314"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:39:20Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:39:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): compute the deploy base in-workflow instead of nx-set-shas (#1520)\n\n* fix(shared): compute the deploy base in-workflow instead of nx-set-shas\n\n`nrwl/nx-set-shas@v5` twice picked a base 78 commits and 25 days stale\n(2026-09-15, 2026-09-16). Because `nx.json` sits in the `sharedGlobals` named\ninput, that wide diff invalidates every project, so both merges rebuilt all\neleven containers instead of the one that changed. A third merge the next day\nwas scoped correctly, which is what makes it hard to notice: it is intermittent,\nand a too-wide base looks exactly like a legitimately wide change.\n\nThe action swallows the reason. Its `commitExists` wraps two GitHub API calls in\n`catch { return false }`, so a rate-limit or 5xx is indistinguishable from\n\"commit was rebased away\" and the loop walks silently backwards to an older run.\nIt also only accepts a base within the newest 100 commits of main (a single\nunpaginated page), and ignores the exit status of its own `git cat-file -e`.\n\nReplace it with the equivalent query plus explicit checks:\n\n- the base must exist in the checkout AND be an ancestor of HEAD, so a commit\n  from an abandoned branch cannot name an image that was never deployed from\n  this line of history\n- the base is the CLOSEST valid ancestor, chosen by counting commits, not the\n  first entry the API happens to return. Ordering is the one input this job\n  cannot verify from the inside, so it no longer depends on it. Verified\n  order-independent against the response reversed and shuffled.\n- every rejected candidate prints why, and a base more than 10 commits back\n  raises a warning. The previous failure mode was entirely silent.\n- no usable base still rebuilds everything, unchanged\n\nAlso pass `--base`/`--head` to nx explicitly rather than relying on the env vars\nthe action exported, and read its output with `--json | jq -r`. The bare output\nis a JSON array in some environments and newline-separated in others; the\nclassification loop greps for whole lines, so a JSON array would have matched\nnothing, marked every container unaffected, and re-tagged stale images — the one\ndirection this job must never fail in.\n\n* fix(shared): fail toward rebuild-all when nx affected-detection errors\n\nThe nx call was piped into jq with `|| echo \"\"` on the end. That guard\nbound to the pipeline, whose status is jq''s, and jq exits 0 on empty input,\nso a failed nx produced an empty affected list. Every container was then\nclassified unaffected and the re-tag job copied stale sha-<base> images\nforward, which is the one direction this step must never fail in.\n\nnx now runs on its own line with its exit status checked. On failure it\nwarns and falls back to the existing rebuild-all path, and stderr is no\nlonger discarded so the reason is in the log.\n\nAlso reword the base_sha output comment: it claimed the value is empty on\na rebuild-all run, but it is computed before that branch and is usually\nset. The re-tag job simply does not run when nothing is unaffected.\n\n* fix(shared): route an unparseable nx result into rebuild-all too\n\nThe previous commit checked nx''s exit status but left the jq parse\nunchecked. Under the runner''s bash -e a failed parse aborts the step,\nwhich is loud but leaves nothing deployed. It now takes the same path as\nan nx failure: warn, print the raw output, rebuild every container. jq\nalso insists on a JSON array, so a changed output format cannot pass as\na list of zero projects. An empty array is still the normal docs-only\nresult and is not treated as failure.\n\nAlso in the base-selection call: keep gh''s stderr so a rate limit or 5xx\nis distinguishable from ''no runs'', and drop the event filter. A run is\nonly success when build, re-tag and deploy all passed or were skipped,\nso a hand-triggered deploy leaves the same complete sha-<HEAD> tag set\nand is as valid a baseline as one chained off the quality pipeline.\n\nThe concurrency comment still named nx-set-shas''s last-successful-event\ninput; it now points at the base selection that replaced it.","tree":{"sha":"a113bed2200e6d51d2001b2648d6069bca9c6bc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/a113bed2200e6d51d2001b2648d6069bca9c6bc5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911","verification":{"payload":"tree a113bed2200e6d51d2001b2648d6069bca9c6bc5\nparent d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789727960 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789727960 +0000\n\nfix(shared): compute the deploy base in-workflow instead of nx-set-shas (#1520)\n\n* fix(shared): compute the deploy base in-workflow instead of nx-set-shas\n\n`nrwl/nx-set-shas@v5` twice picked a base 78 commits and 25 days stale\n(2026-09-15, 2026-09-16). Because `nx.json` sits in the `sharedGlobals` named\ninput, that wide diff invalidates every project, so both merges rebuilt all\neleven containers instead of the one that changed. A third merge the next day\nwas scoped correctly, which is what makes it hard to notice: it is intermittent,\nand a too-wide base looks exactly like a legitimately wide change.\n\nThe action swallows the reason. Its `commitExists` wraps two GitHub API calls in\n`catch { return false }`, so a rate-limit or 5xx is indistinguishable from\n\"commit was rebased away\" and the loop walks silently backwards to an older run.\nIt also only accepts a base within the newest 100 commits of main (a single\nunpaginated page), and ignores the exit status of its own `git cat-file -e`.\n\nReplace it with the equivalent query plus explicit checks:\n\n- the base must exist in the checkout AND be an ancestor of HEAD, so a commit\n  from an abandoned branch cannot name an image that was never deployed from\n  this line of history\n- the base is the CLOSEST valid ancestor, chosen by counting commits, not the\n  first entry the API happens to return. Ordering is the one input this job\n  cannot verify from the inside, so it no longer depends on it. Verified\n  order-independent against the response reversed and shuffled.\n- every rejected candidate prints why, and a base more than 10 commits back\n  raises a warning. The previous failure mode was entirely silent.\n- no usable base still rebuilds everything, unchanged\n\nAlso pass `--base`/`--head` to nx explicitly rather than relying on the env vars\nthe action exported, and read its output with `--json | jq -r`. The bare output\nis a JSON array in some environments and newline-separated in others; the\nclassification loop greps for whole lines, so a JSON array would have matched\nnothing, marked every container unaffected, and re-tagged stale images — the one\ndirection this job must never fail in.\n\n* fix(shared): fail toward rebuild-all when nx affected-detection errors\n\nThe nx call was piped into jq with `|| echo \"\"` on the end. That guard\nbound to the pipeline, whose status is jq''s, and jq exits 0 on empty input,\nso a failed nx produced an empty affected list. Every container was then\nclassified unaffected and the re-tag job copied stale sha-<base> images\nforward, which is the one direction this step must never fail in.\n\nnx now runs on its own line with its exit status checked. On failure it\nwarns and falls back to the existing rebuild-all path, and stderr is no\nlonger discarded so the reason is in the log.\n\nAlso reword the base_sha output comment: it claimed the value is empty on\na rebuild-all run, but it is computed before that branch and is usually\nset. The re-tag job simply does not run when nothing is unaffected.\n\n* fix(shared): route an unparseable nx result into rebuild-all too\n\nThe previous commit checked nx''s exit status but left the jq parse\nunchecked. Under the runner''s bash -e a failed parse aborts the step,\nwhich is loud but leaves nothing deployed. It now takes the same path as\nan nx failure: warn, print the raw output, rebuild every container. jq\nalso insists on a JSON array, so a changed output format cannot pass as\na list of zero projects. An empty array is still the normal docs-only\nresult and is not treated as failure.\n\nAlso in the base-selection call: keep gh''s stderr so a rate limit or 5xx\nis distinguishable from ''no runs'', and drop the event filter. A run is\nonly success when build, re-tag and deploy all passed or were skipped,\nso a hand-triggered deploy leaves the same complete sha-<HEAD> tag set\nand is as valid a baseline as one chained off the quality pipeline.\n\nThe concurrency comment still named nx-set-shas''s last-successful-event\ninput; it now points at the base selection that replaced it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrRTYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEvUQAEyy8b3WjjBqm7xe7jraD0C5\nnLDLLBprOMjm7qlp+WJtIWOiMk+PJrSWwjkHZTPeK44ZHXFKHb5caHptd5xQ4lzL\njI+lbid6ML2ZbFbAhfK+Lz5jK2ARoJ2Xx5HsqD51ivjk9Gg8WrxZdlQeBEUmAuuz\ng+uaHNLHAUgJh6cY5v/16hi/rN752ud3J1dbquW+e7pHRifZqR1BHOoiTT+2YB/u\nOI3xxBmsTUgxec/ZsHBQe+lOlLZWC12Qv2az2ImF1oYr0JH0JZb7h2JMjdTvW188\n1Qd8dNyKXYIK3QzT8LImGFb/1ziGf8+GZlyrrTlElhFKy9sogh853sLF0OTSmJw2\nOX6gQRqqx9VrUXXjdA3ONYHWgic75hTy4wJ6d1cY9X5BVqH/ODP8g5zeSLGWb8M4\nMWe2NTy5wsz37xJzN5IJWcslL+HYJLI8JfJvAu3uia5nGwzKn7pyhwf5ducyz/i7\nHp6VtHWdPKEpdepGpSKaeTan8MQniFPIB75MkFZTsggVcfStWT2PodeMUDzSbEWJ\nd37TnpCDadE0xDeGld3dgFK8yFXXS276wKYpSuNDn7a4lO6pJfWLmeI5LnGUCxE3\n7k/1lpi6lJ3hBI1zZ1Gj1jwC83mZGy6ZaFg31jbY1BlH+VZlogxqvIoLSq4svkuz\nNlcvTvfJZHxPeIdQEZP0\n=khJK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T10:39:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKDU3NDY0OGNmNDAyOWVjMzk1ZDg5NDkwM2Y5NjYxYzdmODEyN2Y5MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c","sha":"d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c"}],"sha":"574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/574648cf4029ec395d894903f9661c7f8127f911"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:32:54Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:32:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(lg): lift DTOs out of the model cycle and guard every entry order (#1516)\n\n* fix(lg): lift DTOs out of the model cycle and guard every entry order\n\nCloses #1506.\n\nEvery `@Api*` decorator argument is read at class-decoration time. When the\ndeclaring module and the argument''s module sit in a value-level import cycle,\nthat read fires mid-evaluation: `undefined` under tsc (a silently wrong Swagger\nschema and no class-transformer nesting), a TDZ `ReferenceError` under swc.\n\n#1505 fixed this for `type-categories` and left `advert.model.ts` for later.\nExtraction of the advert DTOs alone was not enough - `ApplicationDto.adverts`\nneeds `AdvertDto` at value level and `advert.model.ts` imports `ApplicationModel`\nback, which would have pulled `advert.dto.ts` straight back into the cycle. So\n`AdvertDetailedDto`/`AdvertDto`/`ExternalAdvertDto` move to `advert.dto.ts` and\n`ApplicationDto`/`ApplicationDetailedDto` to `application.dto.ts`; the model\nfiles keep them as type-only mapper return types.\n\n`model-cycle.spec.ts` now brute-forces the property a hand-written pin cannot\nexpress: for each `*.model.ts` / `*.dto.ts` it resets the module registry,\nrequires that file first, and asserts every eager decorator argument still\nresolves to the class it names. That matrix found three more defects on main\nthat #1506 did not know about:\n\n- `comment.model.ts` carried a bare `@ApiProperty({ type: StatusDto })`, which\n  is just as eager as `@ApiDto` and which a grep for `@Api*Dto(` never matched.\n- `foreclosure.model.ts` carried `@ApiDtoArray(ForeclosurePropertyDto)` inside a\n  cycle. The `*Array` variants are not immune: a decorator is a function call,\n  so the argument is evaluated at the call site regardless of the `() => classRef`\n  the decorator stores internally. `models.md` said otherwise; corrected.\n- `core/html/advert-html.ts` read `AdvertVersionEnum.A` at module scope from a\n  module it is in a cycle with. Resolved per call now.\n\nAll three reproduce on main; entering the graph via `status.model`,\n`foreclosure-property.model` or `advert-publication.model` throws there today.\n\nNo runtime logic, DTO shape or exported class name changes. Verified by dumping\n`swagger/apiModelProperties` for all 52 classes under `models/` before and\nafter: byte-identical, key order included. 46 suites / 760 tests pass, and the\nguard was confirmed to go red when one fix is reverted.\n\nSwept the rest of the repo while here: of the 49 eager arguments outside this\ndirectory (48 DoE, 1 OJOI), none sits in a cycle - 27 are same-file, 22 cross\nfiles that do not import back. Recorded in `models.md` so nobody re-runs it.\n\n* fix(lg): close the review gaps in the model-cycle guard\n\nAddresses the two should-fix findings on #1516, plus three of the optional ones.\n\n- `model-cycle.spec.ts` still carried the claim this PR exists to disprove: that\n  `TypeWithCategoriesDto` was safe because the `@ApiDtoArray` thunk defers the\n  read. It is safe because `type-categories.dto.ts` sits outside the cycle.\n  Leaving the wrong rule next to the corrected one is how it gets re-learned.\n- `type-categories.dto.ts` was the only file under `models/` whose eager sites\n  were missing from `EAGER_SITES` - the file the original #1505 defect lived in,\n  covered only by a block that pins one import order. Three rows added.\n- `resolveType` branched on `isArray`, so a plain\n  `@ApiProperty({ type: X, isArray: true })` would have thrown \"Class\n  constructor cannot be invoked without ''new''\" instead of failing readably. It\n  now branches on \"non-class function\".\n- The matrix also sweeps every exported class in the directory, so an eager site\n  nobody remembers to register is still exercised. The explicit table stays: its\n  identity check is stronger than a not-undefined check.\n- `models.md` framed the rule around `@Api*Dto` and class references, but the\n  `advert-html.ts` defect was an *enum* read. Widened to any class or enum\n  argument, and the grep that finds bare `@ApiProperty({ type: X })` is recorded\n  so the next count is not another undercount.\n\nNot taken: dropping `version ?? defaultVersion()` in `advert-html.ts`. The\nparameter default only substitutes for `undefined` while `??` also catches\n`null`, so removing it is a behaviour change, and this PR guarantees none.\n\nRe-verified the guard both ways: adding a value-level `comment.dto` import to\n`status.model.ts` turns every entry point red, and reverting it turns all 35\ngreen. Note that under `@swc/jest` the signal is the require throwing rather\nthan the undefined check - a first canary that nulled only the decorator\nargument passed, because `emitDecoratorMetadata` backfills `type` from\n`design:type`. The sweep''s comment now says so instead of overclaiming.","tree":{"sha":"a316d18bb09f74eb1f9e66fbe8a1b18966fdc1f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/a316d18bb09f74eb1f9e66fbe8a1b18966fdc1f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c","verification":{"payload":"tree a316d18bb09f74eb1f9e66fbe8a1b18966fdc1f4\nparent b8ad7f0792ec05108d67433fad1a1031b127887c\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789723974 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789723974 +0000\n\nfix(lg): lift DTOs out of the model cycle and guard every entry order (#1516)\n\n* fix(lg): lift DTOs out of the model cycle and guard every entry order\n\nCloses #1506.\n\nEvery `@Api*` decorator argument is read at class-decoration time. When the\ndeclaring module and the argument''s module sit in a value-level import cycle,\nthat read fires mid-evaluation: `undefined` under tsc (a silently wrong Swagger\nschema and no class-transformer nesting), a TDZ `ReferenceError` under swc.\n\n#1505 fixed this for `type-categories` and left `advert.model.ts` for later.\nExtraction of the advert DTOs alone was not enough - `ApplicationDto.adverts`\nneeds `AdvertDto` at value level and `advert.model.ts` imports `ApplicationModel`\nback, which would have pulled `advert.dto.ts` straight back into the cycle. So\n`AdvertDetailedDto`/`AdvertDto`/`ExternalAdvertDto` move to `advert.dto.ts` and\n`ApplicationDto`/`ApplicationDetailedDto` to `application.dto.ts`; the model\nfiles keep them as type-only mapper return types.\n\n`model-cycle.spec.ts` now brute-forces the property a hand-written pin cannot\nexpress: for each `*.model.ts` / `*.dto.ts` it resets the module registry,\nrequires that file first, and asserts every eager decorator argument still\nresolves to the class it names. That matrix found three more defects on main\nthat #1506 did not know about:\n\n- `comment.model.ts` carried a bare `@ApiProperty({ type: StatusDto })`, which\n  is just as eager as `@ApiDto` and which a grep for `@Api*Dto(` never matched.\n- `foreclosure.model.ts` carried `@ApiDtoArray(ForeclosurePropertyDto)` inside a\n  cycle. The `*Array` variants are not immune: a decorator is a function call,\n  so the argument is evaluated at the call site regardless of the `() => classRef`\n  the decorator stores internally. `models.md` said otherwise; corrected.\n- `core/html/advert-html.ts` read `AdvertVersionEnum.A` at module scope from a\n  module it is in a cycle with. Resolved per call now.\n\nAll three reproduce on main; entering the graph via `status.model`,\n`foreclosure-property.model` or `advert-publication.model` throws there today.\n\nNo runtime logic, DTO shape or exported class name changes. Verified by dumping\n`swagger/apiModelProperties` for all 52 classes under `models/` before and\nafter: byte-identical, key order included. 46 suites / 760 tests pass, and the\nguard was confirmed to go red when one fix is reverted.\n\nSwept the rest of the repo while here: of the 49 eager arguments outside this\ndirectory (48 DoE, 1 OJOI), none sits in a cycle - 27 are same-file, 22 cross\nfiles that do not import back. Recorded in `models.md` so nobody re-runs it.\n\n* fix(lg): close the review gaps in the model-cycle guard\n\nAddresses the two should-fix findings on #1516, plus three of the optional ones.\n\n- `model-cycle.spec.ts` still carried the claim this PR exists to disprove: that\n  `TypeWithCategoriesDto` was safe because the `@ApiDtoArray` thunk defers the\n  read. It is safe because `type-categories.dto.ts` sits outside the cycle.\n  Leaving the wrong rule next to the corrected one is how it gets re-learned.\n- `type-categories.dto.ts` was the only file under `models/` whose eager sites\n  were missing from `EAGER_SITES` - the file the original #1505 defect lived in,\n  covered only by a block that pins one import order. Three rows added.\n- `resolveType` branched on `isArray`, so a plain\n  `@ApiProperty({ type: X, isArray: true })` would have thrown \"Class\n  constructor cannot be invoked without ''new''\" instead of failing readably. It\n  now branches on \"non-class function\".\n- The matrix also sweeps every exported class in the directory, so an eager site\n  nobody remembers to register is still exercised. The explicit table stays: its\n  identity check is stronger than a not-undefined check.\n- `models.md` framed the rule around `@Api*Dto` and class references, but the\n  `advert-html.ts` defect was an *enum* read. Widened to any class or enum\n  argument, and the grep that finds bare `@ApiProperty({ type: X })` is recorded\n  so the next count is not another undercount.\n\nNot taken: dropping `version ?? defaultVersion()` in `advert-html.ts`. The\nparameter default only substitutes for `undefined` while `??` also catches\n`null`, so removing it is a behaviour change, and this PR guarantees none.\n\nRe-verified the guard both ways: adding a value-level `comment.dto` import to\n`status.model.ts` turns every entry point red, and reverting it turns all 35\ngreen. Note that under `@swc/jest` the signal is the require throwing rather\nthan the undefined check - a first canary that nulled only the decorator\nargument passed, because `emitDecoratorMetadata` backfills `type` from\n`design:type`. The sweep''s comment now says so instead of overclaiming.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrQVGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAri8QAJuuoZaESNMJjLl2Ds6xAomO\nEDEZpl1FeA1Tu5Vmr9rnFRWNAZUg//5pzj5QP6/DpYQ2PJ8WekXZyr/l1d0tiSeQ\nL5731DmPkyCLvsvdAkvkFla03rt0xHt+1rqYEdZHUijDSIEpp3wZOF0wsL51thFL\nbCyxOwf7x8Gv98DMqoOZGp4B2fvdKa32f7ge9mycR2oJaFdzP/FqLo2kp/21jRYs\n6fGJd+QbFcsYRZv3E3HzL5kfFcjWeNg5S2Pdt37anqguDIRMfUBCmu3pq7zkQgs7\nsNXHHDG6YgKjB/eQs35Q3eRrjwQnn8OiNGESzSs7KxzSWnhgavFXU1sBHW2Kl7YR\nwEgmNXGA7LU+qVXkiu842M05truYDqzBKVN+VY9DG/TD+P1dzncPFgoWdmtruBF9\n0aN5pmKU66rUPu3ZLz8s2Q+lemSDZLOgPcDdmzWQOW1rMEw2aJtwPuDudJpCTMk6\nQOajS06KcmJy+Ukoqa07vGqokdkSpXd9DDTUASspCAk/xlROaXX2mm8j+YvNJ6vQ\nb+ee1HXgQzuddIPTMtc9Oxb9nqdAfvN477NNNlLTmsMsoAhMAVcq3+GGO199YeBP\njnZJck3Nx9XUdeF0pGNZ/e2x+5dWrQlag8ogQMqEQ97FGz32iKyoFCGWQ6BNbsGK\nya3FARn5DZdlHso8a0kh\n=MIIj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T09:32:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGQ4YmIyYmIxNjcwYjViMjFlNmI2NjRmZTU1ZmVmOGU3NGJmNTJmMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/b8ad7f0792ec05108d67433fad1a1031b127887c","sha":"b8ad7f0792ec05108d67433fad1a1031b127887c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/b8ad7f0792ec05108d67433fad1a1031b127887c"}],"sha":"d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/d8bb2bb1670b5b21e6b664fe55fef8e74bf52f0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24840451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thordurhhh","id":24840451,"login":"thordurhhh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODQwNDUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thordurhhh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/b8ad7f0792ec05108d67433fad1a1031b127887c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:51:37Z","email":"tolleinn@gmail.com","name":"Þórður H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:51:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(doe): normalise report deadlines to day boundaries (#1519)\n\nDue dates ran to whatever time of day a report happened to be approved, so a\ncompany fell out of compliance at 14:20 on a day it was still covered through,\nand the salary renewal window opened mid-day on the date shown to the applicant\n(23:59:59 for companies migrated from the retired register, which named a date\nand then refused all of it bar the last second).\n\n`validUntil` — and the `company.next_*_report_due_at` it is mirrored onto — now\nends the day it names; `earliestSubmissionDate` starts the day it names. Not\nbackfilled: migrated rows were already end-of-day, the few approved since are\ncorrected by hand.\n\nAlso declares the 409 that `POST application/reports/salary` already returns,\nwith its three actual causes, and notes that the renewal gate runs in prod only.","tree":{"sha":"af248ab4d4b0199e6778b7995d6db404d6cc4a89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/af248ab4d4b0199e6778b7995d6db404d6cc4a89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/b8ad7f0792ec05108d67433fad1a1031b127887c","verification":{"payload":"tree af248ab4d4b0199e6778b7995d6db404d6cc4a89\nparent e897336f4da5ceb8ab03da882261f4f32fdca02b\nauthor Þórður H <tolleinn@gmail.com> 1789642297 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789642297 +0000\n\nfix(doe): normalise report deadlines to day boundaries (#1519)\n\nDue dates ran to whatever time of day a report happened to be approved, so a\ncompany fell out of compliance at 14:20 on a day it was still covered through,\nand the salary renewal window opened mid-day on the date shown to the applicant\n(23:59:59 for companies migrated from the retired register, which named a date\nand then refused all of it bar the last second).\n\n`validUntil` — and the `company.next_*_report_due_at` it is mirrored onto — now\nends the day it names; `earliestSubmissionDate` starts the day it names. Not\nbackfilled: migrated rows were already end-of-day, the few approved since are\ncorrected by hand.\n\nAlso declares the 409 that `POST application/reports/salary` already returns,\nwith its three actual causes, and notes that the renewal gate runs in prod 