mr.is/commits/89b59778e093cccce47688ba12ebc37df781cf28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/c21222712f6dbe0d9839e59c39427e458c000da7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T10:36:13Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T10:36:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(shared): remove the dead \"parallel\": 1 from nx.json (#1512)\n\nNx 22.7.8 does not honour it, and has not for some time. It lives in\ntasksRunnerOptions, which Nx marks @deprecated, and it is overwritten before it\nis ever read:\n\n  command-line-utils.js:128  always assigns nxArgs[''parallel'']; with no\n                             --parallel flag and no NX_PARALLEL the value is\n                             undefined, but the KEY IS PRESENT\n  run-command.js:842-845     {...tasksRunnerOptions.options, ...nxArgs} — the\n                             present-but-undefined key clobbers the 1\n  run-command.js:863         result.parallel ??= nxJson.parallel — no top-level\n                             parallel, so no fallback fires\n  task-orchestrator.js:1268  undefined -> Number(maxParallel || 3)\n\nVerified by executing Nx''s own getRunnerOptions/getThreadPoolSize against the\nreal nx.json, and confirmed at runtime from CI logs: run 34863309791 ran 23 test\ntasks, sum 399.1s, span 151.0s, max simultaneous 3 and never 4.\n\nIntroduced by 41d10b5a1 \"Config and setup from island.is project\" (2023-12-15),\na 23-file bulk config import — copied in wholesale, not chosen for this repo. No\nincident or rationale behind it.\n\nRemoving it changes nothing today. Leaving it is the risk: it reads as \"we run\ntests serially\", which is false and already misled an investigation into CI test\ntimings. If anyone adds a top-level `parallel`, or Nx tightens that spread, it\ngoes live and serializes 399s of work instead of 151s — a ~2.5x CI regression.\nThe supported knob, if serial execution is ever wanted, is top-level nx.json\n`parallel`.","tree":{"sha":"fc55e776101b89a69d2484e7fec3def21affeaeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/fc55e776101b89a69d2484e7fec3def21affeaeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/c21222712f6dbe0d9839e59c39427e458c000da7","verification":{"payload":"tree fc55e776101b89a69d2484e7fec3def21affeaeb\nparent cfcc0de0af1717870a43c9bb612166da1e3d76da\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789468573 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789468573 +0000\n\nchore(shared): remove the dead \"parallel\": 1 from nx.json (#1512)\n\nNx 22.7.8 does not honour it, and has not for some time. It lives in\ntasksRunnerOptions, which Nx marks @deprecated, and it is overwritten before it\nis ever read:\n\n  command-line-utils.js:128  always assigns nxArgs[''parallel'']; with no\n                             --parallel flag and no NX_PARALLEL the value is\n                             undefined, but the KEY IS PRESENT\n  run-command.js:842-845     {...tasksRunnerOptions.options, ...nxArgs} — the\n                             present-but-undefined key clobbers the 1\n  run-command.js:863         result.parallel ??= nxJson.parallel — no top-level\n                             parallel, so no fallback fires\n  task-orchestrator.js:1268  undefined -> Number(maxParallel || 3)\n\nVerified by executing Nx''s own getRunnerOptions/getThreadPoolSize against the\nreal nx.json, and confirmed at runtime from CI logs: run 34863309791 ran 23 test\ntasks, sum 399.1s, span 151.0s, max simultaneous 3 and never 4.\n\nIntroduced by 41d10b5a1 \"Config and setup from island.is project\" (2023-12-15),\na 23-file bulk config import — copied in wholesale, not chosen for this repo. No\nincident or rationale behind it.\n\nRemoving it changes nothing today. Leaving it is the risk: it reads as \"we run\ntests serially\", which is false and already misled an investigation into CI test\ntimings. If anyone adds a top-level `parallel`, or Nx tightens that spread, it\ngoes live and serializes 399s of work instead of 151s — a ~2.5x CI regression.\nThe supported knob, if serial execution is ever wanted, is top-level nx.json\n`parallel`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqR+dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUsYQAC0zhJwq+kIFn3ar059m3V9D\nPaoH40cFaWYus0PeUwzlyTdIyki0sozThxdd9chDC+rfs1XFm85ubp2NDuw8kscV\nhTpSb7E6sZ3AYdXX5gtVfVgBDPeTfOC0PFaHuwpHVIVENHno4eQiIgvCTmhmWiOM\nE/yHmiVuy9rwx1rNosAt91jb8tzyA33d3F1p+qT0nv5IMzJD55wJ1DZhFdFuoA8R\nrjYtFpy1MjAnCf9NXUno0vDZ13yhvF42h5oK2nK37fUO6qxSpKE1Ew3fOqqvbvWd\nzXJkHNakL3qFpV68ZD34JqGOiOhem1FqLcpOG3dPXm4gMTCkeNOY3fCsbfOnxchm\nZcpj2j9PKRd+DfE9pYv3YadPNeGvS+WS4IGfHCYNgjPnH7YbmeSK7rAVwLHorXEr\nslwuBM71vLvqkHmH6NufLQypDH57O0o3GT5aEJZikqhkxU7KSCZ4CNOpLApnIZpU\n6aQJpaEWb4nkBMuy+RkkhEbaCDEcRGWzBB0yE9ryCYlf+z4g+8EhDpShHvzS2DtD\ncWwzAP90Iax20Y4TiV20oNQQeZDG08Cy5siLdCve/QBAIMNmSWcFBqUHT6BNCOX9\nxL7ano+4yvv6xET2IhcC7Te3UzmFu4kWW+yCymyBE37JqtKbvbMjS6vMzLEJ/E2J\nYzvf0+e+pF9UMoqHM0m0\n=OvvP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T10:36:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/c21222712f6dbe0d9839e59c39427e458c000da7","node_id":"C_kwDOKxEuldoAKGMyMTIyMjcxMmY2ZGJlMGQ5ODM5ZTU5YzM5NDI3ZTQ1OGMwMDBkYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/DMR-is/dmr.is/commit/cfcc0de0af1717870a43c9bb612166da1e3d76da","sha":"cfcc0de0af1717870a43c9bb612166da1e3d76da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/cfcc0de0af1717870a43c9bb612166da1e3d76da"}],"sha":"c21222712f6dbe0d9839e59c39427e458c000da7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/c21222712f6dbe0d9839e59c39427e458c000da7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9976684?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kthorri","id":9976684,"login":"kthorri","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzY2ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kthorri","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/commits/cfcc0de0af1717870a43c9bb612166da1e3d76da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T10:17:02Z","email":"kristinn.thorri@gmail.com","name":"Kristinn Þorri"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T10:17:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): pin Homebrew/actions to a SHA, unblocking prod deploys (#1511)\n\nBoth prod deploy jobs in the v1.90.0 release failed within 7 seconds with\n\"Unable to resolve action `homebrew/actions@master`, unable to find version\n`master`\". Homebrew deleted that branch in Homebrew/actions#934 on 2026-09-13,\nand GitHub Actions does not follow the rename redirect, so every `@master`\nreference became a hard error.\n\nThe v1.89.0 run on 2026-09-11 already logged the upstream warning added in\nHomebrew/actions#838: \"The ''master'' branch sync will stop and this warning will\nbecome an error.\"\n\nPinned to the full SHA of CalVer tag 2026.09.13.1 rather than `@main`. The\nHomebrew 7.0.0 release notes list `@main` as \"migration recommended\" to a CalVer\nrelease or full SHA, so `@main` would only defer this change. A SHA also keeps\nthe production deploy path off a branch that moves between releases.\n\nThe `gems-path` and `gems-hash` outputs consumed by the RubyGems cache step are\nidentical at this SHA to the last `master` commit the 2026-09-11 deploy ran.","tree":{"sha":"0693dd312156b4584f1db6f3662803b1725cf08e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/trees/0693dd312156b4584f1db6f3662803b1725cf08e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DMR-is/dmr.is/git/commits/cfcc0de0af1717870a43c9bb612166da1e3d76da","verification":{"payload":"tree 0693dd312156b4584f1db6f3662803b1725cf08e\nparent 27cfc0a15cd15e867d4a769a3c8ac36149aedb06\nauthor Kristinn Þorri <kristinn.thorri@gmail.com> 1789467422 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789467422 +0000\n\nfix(shared): pin Homebrew/actions to a SHA, unblocking prod deploys (#1511)\n\nBoth prod deploy jobs in the v1.90.0 release failed within 7 seconds with\n\"Unable to resolve action `homebrew/actions@master`, unable to find version\n`master`\". Homebrew deleted that branch in Homebrew/actions#934 on 2026-09-13,\nand GitHub Actions does not follow the rename redirect, so every `@master`\nreference became a hard error.\n\nThe v1.89.0 run on 2026-09-11 already logged the upstream warning added in\nHomebrew/actions#838: \"The ''master'' branch sync will stop and this warning will\nbecome an error.\"\n\nPinned to the full SHA of CalVer tag 2026.09.13.1 rather than `@main`. The\nHomebrew 7.0.0 release notes list `@main` as \"migration recommended\" to a CalVer\nrelease or full SHA, so `@main` would only defer this change. A SHA also keeps\nthe production deploy path off a branch that moves between releases.\n\nThe `gems-path` and `gems-hash` outputs consumed by the RubyGems cache step are\nidentical at this SHA to the last `master` commit the 2026-09-11 deploy ran.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqRseCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1p0QABVGNDohV8HNhhMkfh7s9Imv\nNunfOFA38hb1JcDca7Ybdti65u8wXKtSfyL0PXuT9A5d+ubHzBvmQchwA+3NbX8j\nSdn0E/lBzD3J2uLzHp7XGcxUxKRZ0Q7I6Yypw9phJ6sqYPGCXGP2DY1D1Z5uA0GJ\nHgULkBvAnD0mwh2bTMKom2XGXAFU1o5Ck7FG1Qa3TLGMHsemCfpj5elM7tIPIZOa\ngOLzVsLYETf3v0Ow6Xn11apVhXi8V+RlrkNZjJ2jNsNWALQIqq4cicOc0ZbNplbT\n3Mc+BqGvTs4V5VeJaR3h68fa5DWiSeqJGotFkCT6Za4LL6SXUS/y7jJV6hv